{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm","id":1398566,"title":"Tell me about The Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-24T02:34:38-07:00","id":1398566,"title":"Tell me about The Realm","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I've always had trouble reading settings with lots of historical and technical details about factions and such, so I'm really sad to have 0 motivation to read about DB society in DB:WFHW and The Realm. I feel like I'm reading too much trivia and I just can't keep concentrating or memorize them. So I thought if I could simply discuss it with people, and see what they liked about this specific part of the setting it would stick better in my mind. <br /> <br /> So the concept is quite simple : Tell me one of the thing that marked you the most, that you prefer, or that you really want to share, about The Realm functioning (may be about Houses, the History of The Realm, its administration, etc ...)<br /> <br /> I'll start with one thing : I love all the dramatic way DB parents have to &quot;neglect&quot; the emotional well-being of their children in order to make them into responsible leaders. It's extremely tragic but very touching and at the same time completely disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T04:37:44-07:00","id":1398579,"title":"","content":"On the one hand: I hate these kinds of threads because they invariably lead to overlooking nuance and creating memeification.<br /> <br /> On the other hand: I love these kinds of threads. I'm in.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> On parenting: this isn't so dissimilar from real world societies. From Communist communes to Spartan Agoge: The State recognises the Child as its most malleable citizen, and the family as the most direct obstacle. Layer on mystic eugenics and build your empire on the ruins of a clan-centric Shogunate... and I don't see how you could end up with anything else.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> One thing I like: The Realm holds the centre of the world.<br /> <br /> It's a wealthy, propserous, cultured empire. They have access to resources and amenities (which we might come to later), that most city-states and Threshold kingdoms do not. Theirs is an elite and martial culture (built on stolen wealth), and the Realm is the centre of culture and learning (for most of the civilised world).<br /> <br /> It does not directly rule beyond the boarders of the Blessed Isle in the middle of the world, but many neighbouring states (which range from city states to small kingdoms, with smaller states collected together for ease of administration) pay tribute as <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tributary_state\" target=\"_blank\">client states</a>. These &quot;Satrapies&quot; (distinct from real life Satrapies) have their own laws, rulers (who are usually normal mortals, Realm Dynasts being forbidden from ruling Satrapies), customs and the Realm appointed Satrap has very little to do with actually running the state -- they collect the tribute and notionally offer advice to the rulers as viziers. Likewise, whilst the Satrapy will have its own Garision of troops, these are soldiers supplied by the Satrap's Great House -- they're not Realm Legionaires. So far as practicable, the existing military of the client state is kept intact.<br /> <br /> What this means is the Realm is the Blessed Isle. The rest of the setting... well that's not the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-26-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T20:40:40-07:00","id":1398700,"title":"","content":"The Scarlet Empress intentionally designed the Realm not to function without her. The satrapies all technically belong to her, but she leased them to the Great Houses (and held the sole authority to renegotiate or revoke those leases). The senate is designed to gridlock without her intervention. The Great Houses all draw their legitimacy from her bloodline, and several ascended to that status specifically to counter or replace Great Houses that no longer suited her needs. Nobody has access to the Realm Defense Grid but her. House Iselsi, supposedly ruined and destroyed, hung on as infiltrators of high society under the assumption that she'd eventually reinstate them. Her secret police have nobody to report to now.<br /> <br /> Of course, she did grow up in the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate, a governmental system beset by constant wars of succession and rival claims of legitimate authority. One might conclude that she saw what became of a world without a strong central authority, and decided she'd never live in such a world again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T22:45:57-07:00","id":1398713,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a community on the Blessed Isle where the Homeowner\u2019s Association has crazy byzantine laws and requires regular lavish parades to be thrown, lest Anathema Ghosts rise up and murder everyone. It\u2019s really exclusive and being allowed to live there is considered a great honor that can\u2019t be refused, even if you know better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T22:49:25-07:00","id":1398715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398700#post1398700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Empress intentionally designed the Realm not to function without her. The satrapies all technically belong to her, but she leased them to the Great Houses (and held the sole authority to renegotiate or revoke those leases). The senate is designed to gridlock without her intervention. The Great Houses all draw their legitimacy from her bloodline, and several ascended to that status specifically to counter or replace Great Houses that no longer suited her needs. Nobody has access to the Realm Defense Grid but her. House Iselsi, supposedly ruined and destroyed, hung on as infiltrators of high society under the assumption that she'd eventually reinstate them. Her secret police have nobody to report to now.<br /> <br /> Of course, she did grow up in the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate, a governmental system beset by constant wars of succession and rival claims of legitimate authority. One might conclude that she saw what became of a world without a strong central authority, and decided she'd never live in such a world again.</div> </div> </div> </div>She\u2019s also a hot take on China\u2019s first emperor, who set up a similar system and decided to live forever, instead of making a stable government with some kind of orderly succession rules. His empire fell apart shortly after he died too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:57:44-07:00","id":1398732,"title":"","content":"Something 3e does with the Blessed Isle to me that stands out is that it's very mcuh a cotninetn in itself for real this time it feels. The Isle is ancient, has had many different polities over the centuries, and the current Scarlet Realm is probably the first time in a long time, if ever, it was united under a single government besides nominal control the Shogunate or Deliberative had. The Empress uniting it wasn't a guarantee as rarely if ever been so. She secured the Grid, but her success after is a matter of good politics, support, luck, and it seems like she honeslty got along well with one of the local potential future rivals (Rawar of Arjuf).<br /> <br /> Kind of a thing wiht 3e also I really like in general i show the Empress' children are discussed in relaitont o the Dynasty more. Mnemon, V'Neef, and Ragara and their views of one-another and their mother is pretty awesome I think. That we also get other children of the Empress about without hosues to thie rname like Beret, Rulinsei and Oban is pretty sweet. Even just that she has a mortal son in Ivoret in the Imperial Palace is a nice touch that adds a lot. And I like that we have more compelxity to the houses, when they were found, and their founders, as well as those who were the Empress children, adoptees, and others and how that all relates together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T06:59:24-07:00","id":1398766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She\u2019s also a hot take on China\u2019s first emperor, who set up a similar system and decided to live forever, instead of making a stable government with some kind of orderly succession rules. His empire fell apart shortly after he died too. </div> </div> </div>The Scarlet Empress is also reminiscent of Empress Dowager Cixi, in that she's deliberately hamstrung her own nation in order to stay in power. The Realm may be the strongest military and economic power in the setting, but its bureaucracy is full of intentionally placed flaws designed to check their ability to function without her as arbiter. She fears military uprisings, so whenever a military house gets too powerful, she orchestrates their downfall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T00:44:15-07:00","id":1398963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398579#post1398579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing I like: The Realm holds the centre of the world.<br /> <br /> It's a wealthy, propserous, cultured empire. They have access to resources and amenities (which we might come to later), that most city-states and Threshold kingdoms do not. Theirs is an elite and martial culture (built on stolen wealth), and the Realm is the centre of culture and learning (for most of the civilised world).<br /> <br /> It does not directly rule beyond the boarders of the Blessed Isle in the middle of the world, but many neighbouring states (which range from city states to small kingdoms, with smaller states collected together for ease of administration) pay tribute as <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tributary_state\" target=\"_blank\">client states</a>. These &quot;Satrapies&quot; (distinct from real life Satrapies) have their own laws, rulers (who are usually normal mortals), customs and the Realm appointed Satrap has very little to do with actually running the state -- they collect the tribute and notionally offer advice to the rulers as viziers. Likewise, whilst the Satrapy will have its own Garision of troops, these are soldiers supplied by the Satrap's Great House -- they're not Realm Legionaires. So far as practicable, the existing military of the client state is kept intact.<br /> <br /> What this means is the Realm is the Blessed Isle. The rest of the setting... well that's not the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>So actually the satrapies are much more independant than I would imagine. It's interesting. But still they have to comply heavily to the Immaculate Order faith I believe ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T00:51:19-07:00","id":1398965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398700#post1398700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Empress intentionally designed the Realm not to function without her. The satrapies all technically belong to her, but she leased them to the Great Houses (and held the sole authority to renegotiate or revoke those leases). The senate is designed to gridlock without her intervention. The Great Houses all draw their legitimacy from her bloodline, and several ascended to that status specifically to counter or replace Great Houses that no longer suited her needs. Nobody has access to the Realm Defense Grid but her. House Iselsi, supposedly ruined and destroyed, hung on as infiltrators of high society under the assumption that she'd eventually reinstate them. Her secret police have nobody to report to now.<br /> <br /> Of course, she did grow up in the Dragon-Blooded Shogunate, a governmental system beset by constant wars of succession and rival claims of legitimate authority. One might conclude that she saw what became of a world without a strong central authority, and decided she'd never live in such a world again.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens technically since her disappearance ? Does these administratives functions stop or were they shared among many pretendants ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T01:54:47-07:00","id":1398974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398963#post1398963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So actually the satrapies are much more independant than I would imagine. It's interesting. But still they have to comply heavily to the Immaculate Order faith I believe ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is expected that they adpot the Immaculate Philosophy. But exceptions exist -- Fajad is specifically called out as keeping its old religion. Harborhead is also dominated by Ahlat's cult.<br /> <br /> The Realm also generally incorporates local religious beliefs. If local gods are compliant, then &quot;Oestra&quot; becomes &quot;Easter&quot; and life goes on as normal complete with Bunny Rabbits and Eggs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:02:07-07:00","id":1398989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398965#post1398965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what happens technically since her disappearance ? Does these administratives functions stop or were they shared among many pretendants ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't know.<br /> <br /> All I can imagine is what would happen if my boss suddenly stopped turning up for work, and there was no-one who could hire someone new.<br /> <br /> I know what MY job is. Whether my boss turns up for work or not, I can clock in, do what I'm supposed to do and go home.<br /> <br /> I kinda know what my boss's job is: at least, I know what they do for me. I know that they send the payroll down each month. I know that if they aren't at work then someone has to send the payroll or I'm not getting paid. I know the hours the team and I work... so even though I've never done a pay run, I reckon I could just take on a little bit more responsibility and get it done.<br /> <br /> But mistakes happen in the pay run. They happened when the boss was here. More are going to happen now. I don't understand the process, so I probably can't fix the problems.<br /> <br /> My boss also has a Tuesday meeting. No idea who with or what for.<br /> <br /> Sally and Rosie hate each other, but the boss put them on the same rota before they disappeared. Do I keep them working together? Do I break them up? What was the plan? Was there a plan?<br /> <br /> If the boss isn't here, who punishes bad behaviour? Who rewards good workers? Who hires? Who fires?<br /> <br /> Now write that on the scale of a continent spanning empire.<br /> <br /> Technically, there's a Regent standing in for the Empress. But he's incompetent. So you have thousands of people like me, all grabbing at their boss's power. Some of them are ambitious back-biters. Some of them are just trying to do their jobs.<br /> <br /> Things aren't going to fall apart overnight. People are sensible. They know their own business.<br /> <br /> But things are going to fall apart.<br /> <br /> Some functions have just stopped working. Only the Empress can make a new magistrate.<br /> <br /> Some have been seized by pretenders. The Imperial Legions have been subsumed by the Great Houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-26-2020, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:47:13-07:00","id":1399001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398732#post1398732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something 3e does with the Blessed Isle to me that stands out is that it's very mcuh a cotninetn in itself for real this time it feels. The Isle is ancient, has had many different polities over the centuries, and the current Scarlet Realm is probably the first time in a long time, if ever, it was united under a single government besides nominal control the Shogunate or Deliberative had. The Empress uniting it wasn't a guarantee as rarely if ever been so. She secured the Grid, but her success after is a matter of good politics, support, luck, and it seems like she honeslty got along well with one of the local potential future rivals (Rawar of Arjuf).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it make sense to keep descendant of ancient cultures/practices on the Blessed Isle, with their rivalries coming back to before the Birth of the Realm, and such ? Or have they been uniformized since the Realm and now they would be very rare occurences ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T05:27:53-07:00","id":1399033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399001#post1399001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it make sense to keep descendant of ancient cultures/practices on the Blessed Isle, with their rivalries coming back to before the Birth of the Realm, and such ?</div> </div> </div> </div>One might assume that the power to change them is also somewhat limited.<br /> <br /> Also that it may have been possible for certain cultures to exist simultaneously without being antagonistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:02:16-07:00","id":1399093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1398963#post1398963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So actually the satrapies are much more independant than I would imagine. It's interesting. But still they have to comply heavily to the Immaculate Order faith I believe ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact Realm Dynasts are forbidden from ruling satrapies. Satrapies govern themselves, but must follow two rules. They must pay tribute to the Realm, which takes the form of anything the Empire specifies, it can be anything from silver to spices to slaves, usually once every two weeks. They must also accept the Immaculate Faith as their official religion and follow it. The satrap is installed with a Realm garrison to ensure those two rules are followed, but otherwise the satrapy does what it likes.<br /> <br /> In return it benefits from imperial military protection, special trade and travel deals with the rest of the empire, immaculates to deal with spirits, and most importantly the Realm wont come and wage war on you. It\u2019s usually a raw deal but the Realm has a BG enough stick that you basically have to take it, although a lot of places become satrapies without any bloodshed. Skilled imperial diplomats can convince people of the benefits, and some places even petition to become a satrapy if they\u2019re in imminent danger and want the support of legions.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think one of my favourite parts of the Realm book relates to the postal service. It\u2019s an absolutely massive network of couriers, mail people, and even semaphore towers that give the Realm a flow of goods and information unprecedented in the second age. They\u2019re also kind of heroes of the people, because a lot of horse riders will take on packages from peasants if they\u2019re already headed in that direction. Plus they have a cool kind of legendary feel to them where you just know there\u2019s tales of a delivery of medicine that a Realm courier had to ride through a stormy mountain pass all night to deliver. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also the all seeing eye is pretty cool. Most of its agents aren\u2019t actually full time spies, which makes sense. There might be a monk or a merchant or a soldier full time, but secretly they\u2019re also reporting to a handler in the Eye. <br /> <br /> <br /> I also love the deliberative. As it was under the empress it was a bit of a puppet just there for show, but now that she\u2019s gone... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/wd-_ygxZoeU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/wd-_ygxZoeU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/wd-_ygxZoeU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/wd-_ygxZoeU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LMYDSyqNpQo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LMYDSyqNpQo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LMYDSyqNpQo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/LMYDSyqNpQo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/s6UbYHCkoZs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/s6UbYHCkoZs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/s6UbYHCkoZs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/s6UbYHCkoZs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which could be pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:42:52-07:00","id":1399098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399093#post1399093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact Realm Dynasts are forbidden from ruling satrapies. Satrapies govern themselves, but must follow two rules. They must pay tribute to the Realm, which takes the form of anything the Empire specifies, it can be anything from silver to spices to slaves, usually once every two weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once or twice A YEAR.<br /> <br /> (The Realm, page 149)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They must also accept the Immaculate Faith as their official religion and follow it. </div> </div> </div>Immaculate <i>Philosophy</i>. (The Realm, page 86.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:27:22-07:00","id":1399102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399098#post1399098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immaculate <i>Philosophy</i>. (The Realm, page 86.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This might look like nit-picking, but the different terms refer to different versions of the religious practice. The Immaculate Philosophy is practiced in the Realm and its satrapies, while the Immaculate Faith (a more personal, less evangelical variant) is practiced in Lookshy. Other variants include the Intou Heresy (Immaculate beliefs + ancestor worship) and Prasad's Pure Way (Immaculate beliefs + Dragon-Blooded as physical gods worthy of direct worship).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:14:18-07:00","id":1399114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399098#post1399098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once or twice A YEAR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh right, I just read Houses of the Bull God and I think their silver caravans go once every two weeks. Twice a year makes a lot more sense for treasure fleet activities and practicality for far off satrapies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T01:47:47-07:00","id":1399533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399033#post1399033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One might assume that the power to change them is also somewhat limited.<br /> <br /> Also that it may have been possible for certain cultures to exist simultaneously without being antagonistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean it like &quot;they necessary are in conflict&quot; but more in a &quot;Is it fair to use it as a good source of depiction of the people in The Blessed Isle or should I make it an exception that is usually tracked down by The Realm&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> Dynasts are forbidden to govern themselves, but I believe each Satrapies belong to a specific House ? Can't we say to an extent that the DB responsible in the House in charge of the Satrapy effectively govern it or am I missing something ?<br /> <br /> Concerning the postal service I think I saw there was a magic road that goes all around the Blessed Isle, allowing for fast and safe travel, etc ... Is it the product of thousands of Terrestrial Circles rituals ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1961_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1961\" data-vbnamecard=\"1961\">Dex Davican</a> Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T02:41:27-07:00","id":1399536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399533#post1399533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean it like &quot;they necessary are in conflict&quot; but more in a &quot;Is it fair to use it as a good source of depiction of the people in The Blessed Isle or should I make it an exception that is usually tracked down by The Realm&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest approaching the Realm's level of control over the people as a spectrum between tight supervision that rapidly arbitrates all disputes and curtails all deviations in the interests of uniformity and harmony and places that are practically the Wild West and of virtually no interest to government or Dynasty so long as their internal disputes don't spill out and they pay a reasonable amount of their taxes. It's a big country with a varied environment to provide different levels of access to those who enforce public order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynasts are forbidden to govern themselves, but I believe each Satrapies belong to a specific House ? Can't we say to an extent that the DB responsible in the House in charge of the Satrapy effectively govern it or am I missing something ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the privilege and duty of the House who is granted the satrapy's lease to ensure that it makes the tribute payments (of which it gets to take a cut) and otherwise remains amenable to the commercial and military interests of the Realm. The purpose of the satrap is to engage with the existing government to keep them informed of Realm wishes and lean on them to comply, to observe the populace for signs of dissent, and to manage the garrison (those troops also provided by the leasing House) for purposes of defence and occasionally directing towards problem elements if the troops of the local magnate prove insufficient to the task. In all other respects, the satrapy governs itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the postal service I think I saw there was a magic road that goes all around the Blessed Isle, allowing for fast and safe travel, etc ... Is it the product of thousands of Terrestrial Circles rituals ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Coastal Road is a piece of infrastructure that survives from the First Age.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T10:25:07-07:00","id":1399615,"title":"","content":"Another cool thing about the Realm: they have Judge Dee-esque Magistrates empowered to investigate crimes and enforce justice. The Magistrates were all appointed personally by the Empress, and many were outcastes, or convicts offered pardons if they took the job. As a result, Magistrates are a varied bunch of legally-sanctioned Dragon-Blooded vigilantes who are primarily loyal to the Empress. They assemble teams of useful mortals called Archons to help with their investigations and tip the Magistrates off to crimes that need investigating. Of course, with the Empress gone, nobody's choosing new Magistrates, and the remaining Magistrates don't have the Empress' protection any more.<br /> <br /> I don't remember if this was specifically in the book, but knowing how the Empress does things, I'm sure that she chose many Magistrates based partially on who they'd most inconvenience. A disowned and resentful member of a troublesome family is extremely useful for keeping that family in check, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T10:52:38-07:00","id":1399620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399615#post1399615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another cool thing about the Realm: they have Judge Dee-esque Magistrates empowered to investigate crimes and enforce justice. The Magistrates were all appointed personally by the Empress, and many were outcastes, or convicts offered pardons if they took the job. As a result, Magistrates are a varied bunch of legally-sanctioned Dragon-Blooded vigilantes who are primarily loyal to the Empress. They assemble teams of useful mortals called Archons to help with their investigations and tip the Magistrates off to crimes that need investigating. Of course, with the Empress gone, nobody's choosing new Magistrates, and the remaining Magistrates don't have the Empress' protection any more.<br /> <br /> I don't remember if this was specifically in the book, but knowing how the Empress does things, I'm sure that she chose many Magistrates based partially on who they'd most inconvenience. A disowned and resentful member of a troublesome family is extremely useful for keeping that family in check, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really great summary of the Magistrates thank you ! We played 3-4 All Seeing Eyes members in a very short campaign and we asked help to a Magistrate on the case we were working, it was surely an interesting experience but I didn't grasp their full context until your explanation. You talked about Judge Dee-esque, I quickly checked who he is on Wikipedia, could you give your perspective on this topic ? I think it would be quite enriching I think.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> Thanks for the answer. 1) Thanks for your perspective on The Blessed Isle, I'll keep that in mind.<br /> 2) So the DB in charge will usually keep appropriate distances regarding these matters, except in specific cases which can usually serve as great dramatic moments for stories. It's quite nice.<br /> 3) I think I'm a bit sad about this, I liked the idea of The Realm putting in place this kind of infrastructure, reflecting the idea that one strength of The Realm is that with enough resources and time, they can make cool infrastructures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T11:06:46-07:00","id":1399624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399620#post1399620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really great summary of the Magistrates thank you ! We played 3-4 All Seeing Eyes members in a very short campaign and we asked help to a Magistrate on the case we were working, it was surely an interesting experience but I didn't grasp their full context until your explanation. You talked about Judge Dee-esque, I quickly checked who he is on Wikipedia, could you give your perspective on this topic ? I think it would be quite enriching I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, I don't have a ton to offer. I've just seen one Judge Dee movie (Judge Dee and the Mystery of the Phantom Flame). He's a wuxia investigator who wields an artifact mace, the ceremonial sign of his legal authority. Since I'm more familiar with extralegal investigators (like many noir heroes), it was interesting to see someone standing as the last incorruptible defender of the Law in a time of great corruption.<br /> <br /> (I think there are problems with that perspective--see Judge Dredd--but it's undeniably appealing to me on an instinctive level.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:32:08-07:00","id":1399650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399615#post1399615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another cool thing about the Realm: they have Judge Dee-esque Magistrates empowered to investigate crimes and enforce justice. The Magistrates were all appointed personally by the Empress, and many were outcastes, or convicts offered pardons if they took the job. As a result, Magistrates are a varied bunch of legally-sanctioned Dragon-Blooded vigilantes who are primarily loyal to the Empress. They assemble teams of useful mortals called Archons to help with their investigations and tip the Magistrates off to crimes that need investigating. Of course, with the Empress gone, nobody's choosing new Magistrates, and the remaining Magistrates don't have the Empress' protection any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 on this. Magistrates are great, they offer tonnes of story hooks and slot into so many different types of games.<br /> <br /> Think the passage Dex is referencing is this one from p.45 in <i>The Realm</i>:<br /> <br /> <i>Every magistrate is Dragon-Blooded. The Empress often chose influential rebels and heretics, relatively harmless criminals, and other social or political outcasts as magistrates \u2014 competent but disgraced Exalted who\u2019d fallen victim to Dynastic machinations, or become scapegoats for grievous failures or personal transgressions against families and rivals. Primarily, the Empress required her magistrates to be savvy, tenacious, talented, concerned with justice, and dependent entirely on her favor for redemption.</i><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Something I really, really like about the Realm in 3e is House Peleps\u2019 ambitions for establishing the Imperial Western Protectorate. Essentially, their response to the Realm Civil War is likely to be forsaking the Blessed Isle entirely, striking out on their own and establishing a new empire in the West.<br /> <br /> It just makes so much sense, in a world that saw Clans Burano and Ophris set a precedent with Prasad and given the fact that supporting the Imperial Navy is INSANELY costly, so much so the House is basically at a \u2018go big or go home\u2019 tipping point. It\u2019s a daring move, one that might fail but one only they are in position to make (I\u2019ve never quite understood why other Houses would be ok with Peleps having the manpower \u2013 marines especially \u2013 that the navy would require, but that\u2019s by the by\u2026) the type of high stakes gamble that screams story options and daring-do.<br /> <br /> The fact it\u2019s an ambition that is largely being held in check by loyalty and patriotism at the highest level just adds another great wrinkle (this on Peleps Lai, head of the Admiralty Board, from page 58 of <i>WFHW</i>, sums it up nicely: <i>She still believes the Empress will return, and won\u2019t entertain the notion of another monarch until convinced otherwise \u2014 and while she\u2019s not as spry as she once was, her martial skills remain sufficient to trounce the occasional upstart who\u2019d defy her. She supports the notion of a Western Empire, though, and dreams of personally presenting this new conquest to the Empress.</i>)<br /> <br /> The whole idea is further explored awesomely in Heirs.<br /> <br /> I could waffle on about the way 3e has enriched the other Great Houses. It's great stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 06-28-2020, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:01:32-07:00","id":1399680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399650#post1399650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just makes so much sense, in a world that saw Clans Burano and Ophris set a precedent with Prasad and given the fact that supporting the Imperial Navy is INSANELY costly, so much so the House is basically at a \u2018go big or go home\u2019 tipping point. It\u2019s a daring move, one that might fail but one only they are in position to make (I\u2019ve never quite understood why other Houses would be ok with Peleps having the manpower \u2013 marines especially \u2013 that the navy would require, but that\u2019s by the by\u2026) the type of high stakes gamble that screams story options and daring-do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the details but I think the Empress intentionally gave them resources and leeway to keep them a thorn in the other Houses' sides... the same way she did for V'neef to make it a thorn in Peleps' side. If that isn't written anywhere then it's just my headcanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:12:42-07:00","id":1399682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399680#post1399680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember the details but I think the Empress intentionally gave them resources and leeway to keep them a thorn in the other Houses' sides... the same way she did for V'neef to make it a thorn in Peleps' side. If that isn't written anywhere then it's just my headcanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own headcanon is the Empress saw House Peleps' monopoly on the navy as a long term potential danger to the security of her power and was probably going to either &quot;nationalize&quot; it a way similar to how she ran the Legions, or was going to start spinning-off fleets to other Houses in the future. V'Neef in this context is kind of the first step in that process that probably was a few centuries long term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T16:29:11-07:00","id":1399689,"title":"","content":"On reflection (if of interest to anyone) the Magistrates seem to stand a bit between A) the Chinese story tradition of morally &quot;upright&quot; heroic magistrate-detectives who investigate crimes and its actual historical experience (county magistrates appointed for short terms outside of their home region), and B) the more Western genre tradition of private investigators, &quot;hardboiled PIs&quot; or &quot;gentleman detective&quot;, who are portrayed as less completely admirable - often eccentric and &quot;picaresque&quot; if not almost anti-heroic - and stand outside of the state and government to a degree. It's an interesting combination of styles!<br /> <br /> (A somewhat similar-in-spirit literary twist is Barry Hughart's Master Li, though that hews a bit more to the private detective template, possibly because Hughart appeared to have some kind of skepticism towards the Confucian social structure and officialdom).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T18:11:19-07:00","id":1399710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399620#post1399620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">3) I think I'm a bit sad about this, I liked the idea of The Realm putting in place this kind of infrastructure, reflecting the idea that one strength of The Realm is that with enough resources and time, they can make cool infrastructures.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Realm has built other things for themselves, a few of which are given descriptions in the eponymous book.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's an indelible premise of the setting that the differences in power between the Exalted and the turning of the ages mean that there are constructions beyond the Dragon Blooded, and when they're gone it's for good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Still, who's the one that holds the Blessed Isle's coast right now? The Solars can build all kinds of nice things for the Dragon Blooded to seize.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399650#post1399650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve never quite understood why other Houses would be ok with Peleps having the manpower \u2013 marines especially \u2013 that the navy would require, but that\u2019s by the by\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious myself as to why that particular aspect of the Realm military structure was originally written like that. Mind, I'm suddenly wondering if it might reflect on some oddities in the organisation of ancient world navies, of which I know little; the most solid point that I have is recollections of Sextus Pompey being able to hold out in Sicily against the Second Triumvirate for a long time on the basis of his independently powerful navy.<br /> <br /> If justifying character reasonings in the context of Third Edition, I'd say Peleps controlling the navy has long been acceptable on the basis of them being one of the oldest Houses, and that it's part and parcel with the sterling reputation they've cultivated. I also imagine that it helps for a navy to end up being a bit less powerful in their world than it is in ours, because Creation has a lot less coastline. And everybody else then gets to shirk the need to pay for the navy's upkeep.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that marines are the kinds of troops that are well drilled for boarding and landing actions and not of much use for anything else. If we're trying to imagine how the setting works logically, I feel as though even the best marines are of little effect against a basically drilled land army. <br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm thinking about the First Punic War, of which I can recall little of the not much I ever examined in detail, seeing as it lacked the flashy features brought by Hannibal and Scipio. But I think it stands out as an example in which powerful navy versus the best land troops of the era was one that ultimately went to the latter. The Carthaginian navy could dominate the Mediterranean but couldn't inflict much grief on the rich heartlands of Italia, and in the end it was easier for Rome to catch up on naval capabilities than it was for their enemies to develop troops that could stand against legions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T18:26:08-07:00","id":1399712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399710#post1399710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm has built other things for themselves, a few of which are given descriptions in the eponymous book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anyone have favorite examples for OP? The premise of this thread suggests they're going to have trouble finding these marvels themself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T00:59:06-07:00","id":1399752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399710#post1399710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that marines are the kinds of troops that are well drilled for boarding and landing actions and not of much use for anything else. If we're trying to imagine how the setting works logically, I feel as though even the best marines are of little effect against a basically drilled land army.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just training, but equipment, animals, and personnel too. Cavalry, heavy infantry, siege equipment, siege engineers, rangers, even logistic support for managing supply lines. <br /> <br /> I matched it out once using best guesses, which is never a good idea in an rpg, and house Peleps marines out number all the legions put together. Those legions would probably crush the marines in pitched land battles. Onthe other hand if you needed soldiers to take a dozen river boats up a stream and enact a lightning raid on some town, that's marines all the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399712#post1399712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have favorite examples for OP? The premise of this thread suggests they're going to have trouble finding these marvels themself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The imperial palace may be the most impressive. Sorcery is wound in spells through every flagstone and doorway, shadowy guardians slip into the space through the mirror, and spirits lurk everywhere. It almost feels like a passage written to say &quot;this is how Lunar assassins don't just kill any dynast with ease&quot;. The palace is also basically a small and supremely luxurious city, filled with plazas and beautiful buildings, there's a tower that contains tiered minageries from all five corners of Creation, entire libraries, theatres and kitchens large enough to roast an elephant are contained within it. <br /> <br /> It's not fantastical in that it's a flying city, or one that fades from the world every 100 years or something, but the sheer scale of it combined with it being so steeped I'm magic is dizzying. You could set an entire campaign in the palace alone and not feel cramped or lacking in interesting new locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T13:13:52-07:00","id":1399902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399712#post1399712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have favorite examples for OP? The premise of this thread suggests they're going to have trouble finding these marvels themself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be another obvious example, but there's also the Heptagram itself, the construction of which was surely no mean feat. Described here from WFHW, p. 87:<br /> <br /> <i>The school itself consists of six towers encircling a seventh in perfect geomantic harmony. Outer towers are filled with laboratories, summoning circles, and rare equipment and materials necessary for magical practice. The central tower contains faculty and student lodgings and the Heptagram\u2019s only lecture hall, wherein each student holds an assigned seat. Food is prepared and the lands maintained by bound elementals and demons, weighted down with wards and geasa to ensure their obedience.</i><br /> <br /> Quite struck by the Balustrade of Glorious Harmony too \u2013 a sorcery academy that's one part peerless manse to one part deliberate mistake-ridden teaching tool:<br /> <br /> <i>A geomantic academy endowed by Mnemon herself, sprawls across a grand stretch of alpine meadow in the mountains above Mnemon-Darjilis. The academy-manse\u2019s architecture is both geomantic marvel and teaching tool, allowing students to observe the seamless flow of Essence from one structure to the next \u2014 and to witness the consequences of shoddy workmanship, through flaws deliberately built into the design. Many residents of the Valley of the Ancients only employ this institution\u2019s graduates, renowned as among Creation\u2019s best, but the greatest honor a student can receive is the right to design a new edifice on the campus.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T03:10:06-07:00","id":1400037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1399650#post1399650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I really, really like about the Realm in 3e is House Peleps\u2019 ambitions for establishing the Imperial Western Protectorate. Essentially, their response to the Realm Civil War is likely to be forsaking the Blessed Isle entirely, striking out on their own and establishing a new empire in the West.<br /> <br /> It just makes so much sense, in a world that saw Clans Burano and Ophris set a precedent with Prasad and given the fact that supporting the Imperial Navy is INSANELY costly, so much so the House is basically at a \u2018go big or go home\u2019 tipping point. It\u2019s a daring move, one that might fail but one only they are in position to make (I\u2019ve never quite understood why other Houses would be ok with Peleps having the manpower \u2013 marines especially \u2013 that the navy would require, but that\u2019s by the by\u2026) the type of high stakes gamble that screams story options and daring-do.<br /> <br /> The fact it\u2019s an ambition that is largely being held in check by loyalty and patriotism at the highest level just adds another great wrinkle (this on Peleps Lai, head of the Admiralty Board, from page 58 of <i>WFHW</i>, sums it up nicely: <i>She still believes the Empress will return, and won\u2019t entertain the notion of another monarch until convinced otherwise \u2014 and while she\u2019s not as spry as she once was, her martial skills remain sufficient to trounce the occasional upstart who\u2019d defy her. She supports the notion of a Western Empire, though, and dreams of personally presenting this new conquest to the Empress.</i>)<br /> <br /> The whole idea is further explored awesomely in Heirs.<br /> <br /> I could waffle on about the way 3e has enriched the other Great Houses. It's great stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fun, because in my first campaign I randomly chose House V'neef to establish themselves in the Dreaming Sea, instead of participating in the Realm Civil War. Happens than Peleps would be the most likely to do it. Is there any mention of their plans or where they would settle in the West ? How they would do it, their objectives, and what problem they would encounter ? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I didn't know the Imperial Palace was so cool ! I definitively should do a campaign in it. I suppose the Palace is constructed in the place where the Empress control the Realm Defense grid ? <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24647_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24647\" data-vbnamecard=\"24647\">Moss Reynholm</a> Is the Balustrade of Glorious Harmony another high school for DB ? I thought the only high school were The Heptagram, the military school and another last one I don't recall. Are there actually more than these 3 ? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T04:29:00-07:00","id":1400044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400037#post1400037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Is the Balustrade of Glorious Harmony another high school for DB ? I thought the only high school were The Heptagram, the military school and another last one I don't recall. Are there actually more than these 3 ? </div> </div> </div> </div>The leading schools are the Heptagram, Spiral Academy, the Cloister of Wisdom, and the House of Bells. Pasiap's Stair exists to give remedial education to Lost Eggs who choose to take the Coin. These are your Ivy League colleges.<br /> <br /> But other, less prestigious schools exist. They are principally attended by mortal Dynasts and wealthy Patricians, but Dragon-Blooded do, occasionally, attend. This is basically community college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T04:58:56-07:00","id":1400050,"title":"","content":"One thing I always liked about the Realm is that the prestige of its highest aristocracy is enshrined, but not based on things that they can just sit on to continuously accumulate easy wealth. Even when they're not in direct service to the Realm (which relatively few of them are), they still need to continuously exert effort and engage in meaningful work to maintain their wealth and status.<br /> <br /> And that is reflected in the schooling. Nobody is given an easy ride through that system based on family background. I like how Third Edition codified the idea that not all Exalted Dynast children are up to the standards that the top secondary schools hold for entrants, and so they need recourse from the lesser schools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:23:23-07:00","id":1400052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400044#post1400044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But other, less prestigious schools exist. They are principally attended by mortal Dynasts and wealthy Patricians, but Dragon-Blooded do, occasionally, attend. This is basically community college.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way some of these schools feel when written is almost like extreme specialist grad programs too. The Mnemon funded geomancer one here seems genuinely in high repute and demand and likely has a largely Exalted body but it has a laser focus on its job. Similarly the Ragara fund an extremely well regarded school that seems laser focused on the use of magic in exploration and prospecting. Both of these feel like a place a DB wouldn't mind boasting being from vs.a second or third tier military academy mostly full of mortal cadets or dragons forbid: Threshold schooling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:55:57-07:00","id":1400060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400050#post1400050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I always liked about the Realm is that the prestige of its highest aristocracy is enshrined, but not based on things that they can just sit on to continuously accumulate easy wealth. Even when they're not in direct service to the Realm (which relatively few of them are), they still need to continuously exert effort and engage in meaningful work to maintain their wealth and status.<br /> <br /> And that is reflected in the schooling. Nobody is given an easy ride through that system based on family background. I like how Third Edition codified the idea that not all Exalted Dynast children are up to the standards that the top secondary schools hold for entrants, and so they need recourse from the lesser schools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying a young Exalted from a prestigious family can't &quot;buy his way&quot; into a prestigious school in Exalted 3e ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:59:38-07:00","id":1400062,"title":"","content":"Buying your way in probably happens, but not as often as people think. Schools like the Heptagram (especially the Heptagram) really are a meritocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":".  Hit the Send button too fast lol 06-30-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:01:50-07:00","id":1400063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse;n1400037[USER=&amp;quot;1121&amp;quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">DrLoveMonkey[/USER] I didn't know the Imperial Palace was so cool ! I definitively should do a campaign in it. I suppose the Palace is constructed in the place where the Empress control the Realm Defense grid</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep that\u2019s the imperial manse, and it is located within the palace grounds. It\u2019s a big squat building that\u2019s surrounded by massive trees. Also as high up as the palace is built, with many, many structures soaring into the sky covered in terraces and balconies, it also has depth. Beneath the paving stones on the ground level there is a labyrinth of deep cellars and vaults full of wonders collected from all over the world and across millennia of time. It\u2019s also so huge that even with the massive amount of stuff crammed in it, there\u2019s a ton of buildings left vacant and unused as their purposes have been taken elsewhere, just waiting for someone to come along and set up shop.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also home to a big population of ministers, government officials, and close friends of the dynasty. As well as the primary barracks for the Silent Legion, which is a group of 5,000 magically enhanced giant mortals who are the empress\u2019s personal guard, kind of like the secret service. They\u2019re so huge they can wield a halberd in one hand, and beyond that, nearly fearless. They also have other more mysterious powers which are left up to Storytellers, such as battle transformations or other magical abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:01:53-07:00","id":1400064,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> nah. Not community college. More like Lake Forest. (NOT Wake Forest.) Schools for rich kids who can\u2019t get in anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:15:36-07:00","id":1400074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400060#post1400060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying a young Exalted from a prestigious family can't &amp;quot;buy his way&amp;quot; into a prestigious school in Exalted 3e ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it\u2019s more that the Realm has a culture that\u2019s extremely demanding of the dynasty. Normally if you\u2019re stupid rich you can basically just pay people to make you more money and be really lazy, as long as some people in your family are doing something you\u2019ll never have to really worry about anything. You can afford to be someone who just gives up and nobody cares. <br /> <br /> In the Realm that\u2019s rare, you get your ass to work. You can get your ass to work on your own personal projects or something, but there is enormous pressure to perform. So much so that you need to fail and fall several times before you get to just flop. If you didn\u2019t get into the best school, go to the second best, or third. If you fail out of that go to your aunt\u2019s estate and try to learn her business from her. If you mess that up you\u2019re going to the military, or to become a monk. If somehow you can\u2019t even do that right maybe a few other things until finally your elders give up on you and you\u2019re pushed away someplace quiet where you can\u2019t do any more damage. Once there you live on the barest dynastic stipend and get shunned by everyone. Which is pretty horrible. Your life is still comfortable, but with no real friends and a family that hates you, you could easily fall into some pretty serious depression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T07:37:06-07:00","id":1400084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400052#post1400052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way some of these schools feel when written is almost like extreme specialist grad programs too. The Mnemon funded geomancer one here seems genuinely in high repute and demand and likely has a largely Exalted body but it has a laser focus on its job. Similarly the Ragara fund an extremely well regarded school that seems laser focused on the use of magic in exploration and prospecting. Both of these feel like a place a DB wouldn't mind boasting being from vs.a second or third tier military academy mostly full of mortal cadets or dragons forbid: Threshold schooling</div> </div> </div> </div>While the four great secondary schools offer an excellent education, their true benefit from the Dynasty's perspective is the political connections they offer to attendees. A student has the opportunity to establish lifelong bonds with any number of other young Dynasts that they can draw upon later on behalf of their family and their house. No amount of specialized education at a lesser secondary school can make up for losing this opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:06:38-07:00","id":1400091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400084#post1400084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the four great secondary schools offer an excellent education, their true benefit from the Dynasty's perspective is the political connections they offer to attendees. A student has the opportunity to establish lifelong bonds with any number of other young Dynasts that they can draw upon later on behalf of their family and their house. No amount of specialized education at a lesser secondary school can make up for losing this opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. Connections are vital to the Dragon-Blooded, and any ambitious Dynast quickly learns the delicate art of networking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:14:14-07:00","id":1400092,"title":"","content":"If I ever played a Dynast I would play a Water or Air Aspected sorceress (or sorcerer) who was a graduate of the Heptagram (not least because being a sorceress saves on sexting costs when your character and their partner are apart \ud83d\ude0a J/K).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:21:03-07:00","id":1400340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400084#post1400084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While the four great secondary schools offer an excellent education, their true benefit from the Dynasty's perspective is the political connections they offer to attendees. A student has the opportunity to establish lifelong bonds with any number of other young Dynasts that they can draw upon later on behalf of their family and their house. No amount of specialized education at a lesser secondary school can make up for losing this opportunity.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I should think that it's also seen as useful to have these things as structured institutions so that your fresh superhumans can grow up socialised and getting used to their powers without, you know... horribly killing each other.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Although that's probably less the kind of benefit that they're built towards and more a case of &quot;this is a necessary standard to which we hold these institutions, and the fact that they pull it off is a mark of their quality&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400060#post1400060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying a young Exalted from a prestigious family can't &quot;buy his way&quot; into a prestigious school in Exalted 3e ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a bit, but not to the degree where their entry standards are rendered purely nominal. The schools are also serving powerful interests that would look askance at such things in excess, and it's kind of contrary to how Dynasts are socialised.<br /> <br /> I was initially a bit reluctant to make that point what with the appointments to command positions of the Imperial Legions newly assigned to the Great Houses, but then recalled how that's not a case of &quot;my kid is getting the best of everything and I have the clout to make that happen regardless of merit&quot; but one of &quot;right now the highest priority is making sure these troops and lower officers are loyal to us, and that means putting family members who'll march them under our orders in command&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T10:38:05-07:00","id":1400344,"title":"","content":"Another Realm-relevant piece of setting info: the Immaculate Order explicitly exists to reinforce (and enforce) the proper social order. Monks collect intelligence, hoard academic knowledge, build community relationships, and hone their bodies into weapons so they can apply the proper pressure to fix any kind of breakdown in the social order. They may preach when that's effective, but as far as they're concerned, how layfolk <i>act</i> is more important than what they <i>believe</i>. This is why they don't generally tell layfolk that the Solar and Lunar Anathema are Exalted--it would only make the Wyld Hunt's inherent tragedy more apparent, when hunters need hard hearts. It may not be a Celestial Exalt's <i>fault</i> that their power will inevitably upset the proper order of things, but the end result is the same, and so they need to be dealt with quickly and efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:38:32-07:00","id":1400534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400037#post1400037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fun, because in my first campaign I randomly chose House V'neef to establish themselves in the Dreaming Sea, instead of participating in the Realm Civil War. Happens than Peleps would be the most likely to do it. Is there any mention of their plans or where they would settle in the West ? How they would do it, their objectives, and what problem they would encounter ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24647_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24647\" data-vbnamecard=\"24647\">Moss Reynholm</a> Is the Balustrade of Glorious Harmony another high school for DB ? I thought the only high school were The Heptagram, the military school and another last one I don't recall. Are there actually more than these 3 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, late to this and other folk have answered lots of it already. Only thing I\u2019ll add is that the write-ups we currently have of the lesser secondary schools do a fine job of emphasising the bits of their curriculum they excel at/make them unique/interesting (\u2018cause they provides the best story hooks\u2026) as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12596_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12596\" data-vbnamecard=\"12596\">Alpharius</a> explains.<br /> <br /> So the Balustrade of Glorious Harmony is geomancy nirvana, the Forge of Mother\u2019s Fury (another sorcery school) is big on weapon-forging (and is \u2018one of the few forges in the Realm licensed to work orichalcum\u2019), while the House of the Whispering Squall is a Threshold academy that apparently educates most of (Cadet) House Ferem\u2019s youngsters.<br /> <br /> One further wrinkle that I really like and <i>think</i> got added to the lore in Heirs (although it may simply be I\u2019ve not registered it before - any one know?) is that you can learn sorcery at any of the iconic academies. It\u2019s detailed in two paragraphs on p.24 if anyone\u2019s interested/missed it, my favourite part of which being the Immaculate sorcerer detail. Spoilered below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <i>The other three great academies, as well as Pasiap\u2019s Stair, maintain limited sorcerous curriculums for those with the talent and inclination. Students at the House of Bells learn war-magic to decimate armies or turn storms against enemy fleets; the Spiral Academy teaches how to loose one\u2019s shadow as a spy or mesmerize with a glance.<br /> <br /> The Cloister of Wisdom hosts the most advanced curriculum, teaching sorcery holistically in accordance with doctrine and the Immaculate Dragons\u2019 wisdom. Immaculate sorcerer-monks endure less of the Realm\u2019s prejudices and fears regarding sorcerers, provided they adhere to the Philosophy in all things \u2014 particularly in their sorcery.</i><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On Peleps, Heirs at the minute has them securing Wu-Jian and Black Gannet Rock, then Wavecrest, Zhaojun and onwards, targeting V\u2019neef holdings wherever possible but also explaining how they could end up fighting against pretty much all of the Western powers if that suits your game.<br /> <br /> Could say loads more (it\u2019s a pretty big chapter) but suspect people will wanna read it all in their own time when it comes fully available. I really enjoyed it \u2013 big thumbs up from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 07-02-2020, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:37:35-07:00","id":1400543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400534#post1400534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One further wrinkle that I really like and <i>think</i> got added to the lore in Heirs (although it may simply be I\u2019ve not registered it before - any one know?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta hit that sweet WP recovery.<br /> <br /> 2E MoEP: The Dragon-Blooded page 24:<br /> <br /> Among the Realm\u2019s Dragon-Blooded, knowledge of one or two spells does not make one a sorcerer. Any Dragon-Blood might learn a single spell, and many make the effort to learn Emerald Countermagic, which most Dynastic schools teach to students who show the aptitude.<br /> <br /> Page 25<br /> <br /> Under the tutelage of House instructors (or much older students) small units drill together practicing armed and unarmed combat, maneuvers, battlefield sorcery and endurance training.<br /> <br /> Page 32/33 has a Cloister Graduate who is a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Compass of Celestial Directions: The Blessed Isle names Ledaal Mazhorie as the sorcery instructor for the House of Bells.<br /> <br /> 1E... less clear. Exalted The Dragon-Blooded makes mention that not all sorcerers are Heptagram graduates, but it doesn't specifically say the other schools teach sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-03-2020, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T10:56:32-07:00","id":1400545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400543#post1400543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta hit that sweet WP recovery.<br /> <br /> 2E MoEP: The Dragon-Blooded page 24:<br /> <br /> Among the Realm\u2019s Dragon-Blooded, knowledge of one or two spells does not make one a sorcerer. Any Dragon-Blood might learn a single spell, and many make the effort to learn Emerald Countermagic, which most Dynastic schools teach to students who show the aptitude.<br /> <br /> Page 25<br /> <br /> Under the tutelage of House instructors (or much older students) small units drill together practicing armed and unarmed combat, maneuvers, battlefield sorcery and endurance training.<br /> <br /> Page 32/33 has a Cloister Graduate who is a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Compass of Celestial Directions: The Blessed Isle names Ledaal Mazhorie as the sorcery instructor for the House of Bells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah, it's not like it's cited really clearly <i>multiple times</i> is it? Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T15:57:17-07:00","id":1400590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400344#post1400344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Realm-relevant piece of setting info: the Immaculate Order explicitly exists to reinforce (and enforce) the proper social order. Monks collect intelligence, hoard academic knowledge, build community relationships, and hone their bodies into weapons so they can apply the proper pressure to fix any kind of breakdown in the social order. They may preach when that's effective, but as far as they're concerned, how layfolk <i>act</i> is more important than what they <i>believe</i>. This is why they don't generally tell layfolk that the Solar and Lunar Anathema are Exalted--it would only make the Wyld Hunt's inherent tragedy more apparent, when hunters need hard hearts. It may not be a Celestial Exalt's <i>fault</i> that their power will inevitably upset the proper order of things, but the end result is the same, and so they need to be dealt with quickly and efficiently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the monks are participants in and guides to volatile expressions of working class frustration is not a new feature of the Realm, but I certainly feel that this Edition gives it some of the most frequent emphasis.<br /> <br /> I found it appropriately sinister as I read it, and that feeling is only being compounded by recent events, in combination with listening to points about how the Malthusian social policies of Victorian Britain led to frequent riots.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order spends the whole time deeply embedding itself within the communities of the Realm's workers even while they're coordinated by leaders that are deeply tied to the interests of the people who benefit from the labours of those workers. Their advocacy for the peasantry can be so easily read as providing them with intermittent, predictable outlets for their growing anger in a manner that is not beyond the power of the rulers to contain it, while also keeping people invested in the benefits provided by an organisation that tells them that the struggles of their station in life are a result of cosmic ordination rather than observable economic trends, and to put up with that struggle will ultimately be rewarded by being graced with the highest positions that benefit from those labouring beneath them, and ultimately a form of transcendence. It's arguably a far more offensive dimension to them than the old chestnut of whether or not their cosmology is factually true.<br /> <br /> Hmm, considering that makes me have to ask... are you <i>sure</i> they regard people's beliefs as a lot less importance than their actions? Like, if you want their actions to consist of labouring predictably in the service of the Realm, do you not want them to believe in your theology of work actually being spiritually liberating and don't question your station in life for anything like high risk high reward endeavours or even challenging the distribution of power?<br /> <br /> One of the Immaculate mandates is for how frequently they need to hear excerpts from the Texts read, is it not? Is the point of that to attempt rational arguments that people may or may not agree with, or to expose them to the kinds of repetitions of propaganda and vocabulary of though-terminating cliches that actually do have measurable effects on the formation of habitual patterns of belief and action?<br /> <br /> (Which is not to say that actually works to nearly the extent that the Realm's leaders would like, I should expect that a lot of peasants are pretty canny to what the game is or can form the kinds of syncretic belief systems that simultaneously hold the values of &quot;it's right that the Dragon Blooded rule over us&quot; and &quot;skim as much off the top of what is paid to them as you can get away with&quot;. Just the possibility that there might be a genuine intention to promote as much of that thought which supports the empire as they can get.)<br /> <br /> The parts of The Realm that I've actually managed to read so far could probably do with a refresher in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:14:55-07:00","id":1400642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400590#post1400590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The parts of The Realm that I've actually managed to read so far could probably do with a refresher in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note:<br /> <br /> How would people feel about an Exalted book club? We all read a chapter of The Realm every week then come to discuss it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:34:45-07:00","id":1400645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400590#post1400590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Order spends the whole time deeply embedding itself within the communities of the Realm's workers even while they're coordinated by leaders that are deeply tied to the interests of the people who benefit from the labours of those workers. Their advocacy for the peasantry can be so easily read as providing them with intermittent, predictable outlets for their growing anger in a manner that is not beyond the power of the rulers to contain it, while also keeping people invested in the benefits provided by an organisation that tells them that the struggles of their station in life are a result of cosmic ordination rather than observable economic trends, and to put up with that struggle will ultimately be rewarded by being graced with the highest positions that benefit from those labouring beneath them, and ultimately a form of transcendence. It's arguably a far more offensive dimension to them than the old chestnut of whether or not their cosmology is factually true.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, agreed. On the other hand, I provide mental healthcare to people deeply in need, <i>and also</i> from some perspectives I am a willing agent of the state, bound to serve its purposes and influence vulnerable people to stabilize the status quo rather than challenging it. Because I'm limited in my power over the world, I feel I must commit some evils (e.g. charging people money, encouraging people to accept small injustices) for the opportunity to do good. The more idealistic, community-minded monks might well think the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, considering that makes me have to ask... are you <i>sure</i> they regard people's beliefs as a lot less importance than their actions? Like, if you want their actions to consist of labouring predictably in the service of the Realm, do you not want them to believe in your theology of work actually being spiritually liberating and don't question your station in life for anything like high risk high reward endeavours or even challenging the distribution of power? </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say belief is <i>a lot</i> less important than action, because they're related. Obedience to the Dragon-Blooded refines mortal souls regardless of the mortals' motivations--Dragon-Blooded commands inherently elevate their inferiors. But people can be incredibly stubborn, and they might need explanation, negotiation, compensation, intimidation, or flattery to do what's in everybody's best interest (that is, obeying the Dragon-Blooded). Belief isn't <i>required</i> among layfolk, but it's <i>very useful</i>. I'm sure many monks consider it the most important, most reliable way to reinforce the social order. It's just not the only strategy to secure right action, and it isn't sufficient for some circumstances--after all, the Anathema can sway mortal beliefs with ease, and threats secure obedience very quickly even among non-Immaculates.<br /> <br /> (As always, a reminder that I don't speak for the devs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 07-03-2020, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T02:47:12-07:00","id":1400670,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1961_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1961\" data-vbnamecard=\"1961\">Dex Davican</a> really cool job. One of my BFFs does that.<br /> <br /> Question (for anyone): is there any real objective truth to the Immaculate Order\u2019s religious beliefs (like Jesus rising from the dead, either it did happen or it didn\u2019t), or are they all basically made up to reinforce the Dynastic social order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T04:54:57-07:00","id":1400697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400670#post1400670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1961_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1961\" data-vbnamecard=\"1961\">Dex Davican</a> really cool job. One of my BFFs does that.<br /> <br /> Question (for anyone): is there any real objective truth to the Immaculate Order\u2019s religious beliefs (like Jesus rising from the dead, either it did happen or it didn\u2019t), or are they all basically made up to reinforce the Dynastic social order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deliberately left ambiguous.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of faith.<br /> <br /> It is a fact that the religion exists to serve the nefarious social aims of the Bronze Faction. The religion also contains falsehoods (such as attributing deeds carried out by the Celestial Exalted to Terrestrials) and allegorical tales that might not be literally true.<br /> <br /> But whether the religion is <i>based on truth</i> (but biased and twisted to suit these social aims) or <i>completely</i> fabriacted (or even perhaps accidently true either by coincidence or Prachet-esque causality) is something for the ST to decide.<br /> <br /> I think the game is more interesting and morally complex if it is based on truth. If you are inventing something, it's easier and more useful to invent something based on truth than to make it up whole cloth.<br /> <br /> As pure headcanon, I think it makes sense if the Primordials structured human reincarnation to reward those who served their masters. And the Dragon-Blooded/Sidereals just glommed onto that. Likewise the Immaculate Philosophy discourages the sorts of behaviour likely to result in Celestial Exaltation... which, from a certain point of view, could be considered &quot;true&quot;. People should receive proper burials so they don't rise as hungry ghosts. Gods shouldn't enslave mortals. (I mean, if you are a moral relativist, you could make the case that people SHOULDN'T receive proper burials so they do rise as hungry ghosts... but most people would agree with the Immaculates here.)<br /> <br /> Obviously YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-03-2020, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:51:00-07:00","id":1400734,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I like your idea. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:32:14-07:00","id":1400744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise the Immaculate Philosophy discourages the sorts of behaviour likely to result in Celestial Exaltation... which, from a certain point of view, could be considered &quot;true&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To some extent *possibly* yes, though with the caveat that the Immaculate Philosophy isn't really the religion of obedience so much as hierarchical relationships - as I understand it, there's as much encouragement for patricians to take charge of peasants and parents for children, and so on, of heroic sort of actions in that role as protector of leaders, as there is obedience to the Dragonblooded. And Celestial Exaltation may grade on a curve if it's looking for potential.<br /> <br /> But also I would caveat that is probably not intended - discouraging Celestial Exaltation among Immaculate believers (even were it possible) just shifts it to barbarian nations not under the Realm, which is perhaps suboptimal for the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T08:53:06-07:00","id":1400751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400744#post1400744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To some extent *possibly* yes, though with the caveat that the Immaculate Philosophy isn't really the religion of obedience so much as hierarchical relationships - as I understand it, there's as much encouragement for patricians to take charge of peasants and parents for children, and so on, of heroic sort of actions in that role as protector of leaders, as there is obedience to the Dragonblooded. And Celestial Exaltation may grade on a curve if it's looking for potential.<br /> <br /> But also I would caveat that is probably not intended - discouraging Celestial Exaltation among Immaculate believers (even were it possible) just shifts it to barbarian nations not under the Realm, which is perhaps suboptimal for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like proof that the Realm needs to bring the perfected hierarchy to these benighted nations as quickly as possible. If fewer Anathema appear on the Blessed Isle (and I\u2019m not sure about that), then the system clearly works, regardless of the specific reasons.<br /> <br /> (I don\u2019t recall anything in the books about an intentional strategy of discouraging heroism in mortals, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 07-03-2020, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:02:03-07:00","id":1400767,"title":"","content":"It should also be said that the Immaculate Order is a lot bigger than just a tool for the Bronze faction to keep things in check. As Dex said it can be good for your mental health to focus on and appreciate things that you have, which is something a lot of religions encourage. If you go through your day deliberately trying to be thankful for things you'd be amazed at how bright the world can be. Your breakfast in the morning has almost zero chance to include a deadly disease or parasite, you made it to work safely through traffic, this elevator took you up several flights of stairs with no problems. Even if there were problems somebody would come and save you. Even if the building was on fire, there are people who would risk their lives to charge into that building and help you get out.<br /> <br /> Even focusing on what you're doing and appreciating the value of it is not bad. If you're a material packager for an elastic string factory, that can be pretty soul crushing. If you learn that those strings are going to a plant to make masks to keep everyone safe from a deadly disease, it may make you feel a bit less awful about going to work and packing boxes all day. It may even lead you to taking initiative and speaking up if you notice that some of the strings have been looking a bit frayed in the last batch.<br /> <br /> The dark side of that is that a monk will tell you that it's your job to stack boxes until you die, and the only way you have of doing anything better than that is by doing well now and dying so you can be reborn as somebody who's not a box packer. That makes me wonder how far a really hardline monk would go with it though. Can a crate packer go become a fisherman, or is that an affront to the hierarchy? What about peasant business owners, should they work hard to make sure their business neither shrinks nor grows? Or is it just that a peasant can never become a patrician or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:30:14-07:00","id":1400774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400767#post1400767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dark side of that is that a monk will tell you that it's your job to stack boxes until you die, and the only way you have of doing anything better than that is by doing well now and dying so you can be reborn as somebody who's not a box packer. That makes me wonder how far a really hardline monk would go with it though. Can a crate packer go become a fisherman, or is that an affront to the hierarchy? What about peasant business owners, should they work hard to make sure their business neither shrinks nor grows? Or is it just that a peasant can never become a patrician or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be an unorthodox position. The Dragons give, and the Dragons take away; it would be extraordinarily cruel if you had to accept all of the places where chance and destiny grind you down, but you had to give up anything that chance and destiny offer that would lift you back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:46:20-07:00","id":1400776,"title":"","content":"To expand, I think that the acceptability of changing one's station is circumstantial.<br /> <br /> If there are not enough crate packers to support local business, then becoming a fisher instead is an abdication of your responsibility to the community. But if there are a surfeit of crate packers and a shortage of fishers, then changing careers benefits the community.<br /> <br /> A peasant business owner whose hard, steady, legitimate work makes her rich has earned her fortune. But if she takes risks that might sink her business \u2014 impoverishing her family and leaving the community without her services \u2014 or if she underpays or otherwise harms her employees, or pollutes the local farmland, or the like, then she's endangering the community.<br /> <br /> If a rich peasant receives an offer of marriage from an impoverished patrician family, it's entirely appropriate for the peasant to accept this offer from a social superior. But using her wealth as a tool to obtain such a marriage \u2014 in service to her own ambition \u2014 might be seen as inappropriate. (But the wealthy and powerful are typically less bound by religious restrictions than those without such resources.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd say that you can use the Five Antitheses as a rule of thumb for what the Immaculate Philosophy deems inappropriate. If a specific behavior isn't covered by any of the Antitheses, it's probably legitimate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 07-03-2020, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:07:17-07:00","id":1400785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400767#post1400767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dark side of that is that a monk will tell you that it's your job to stack boxes until you die, and the only way you have of doing anything better than that is by doing well now and dying so you can be reborn as somebody who's not a box packer. That makes me wonder how far a really hardline monk would go with it though. Can a crate packer go become a fisherman, or is that an affront to the hierarchy?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of gray in social mobility. I'd say that the hardliner might focus less on &quot;changing your profession is an affront to the hierarchy,&quot; and more on arguments like &quot;with your gifts, your community benefits from your physical labor,&quot; or &quot;you've been slacking off at crate-packing, and that dereliction of your duty makes more work for everyone else,&quot; or &quot;there are Anathema nearby and we don't have the luxury of abandoning our posts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ideally, a monk <i>should</i> recognize that a mortal will do more good for the community if they play to their gifts--after all, the monk left their own place in society behind as well. Perhaps the monk hears that a nearby fishing boat is short-crewed, and even helps make the connection for the recalcitrant crate-packer. As custodians of the social order, monks are well-situated and explicitly encouraged to help solve community problems, with a variety of explanations for why the status quo didn't truly reflect the perfected order. People will often seek out monks for just that sort of arbitration and outside-the-box problem-solving, trusting the monks' wisdom, strength, and authority.<br /> <br /> Of course, every organization with some measure of authority has bullies. In peaceful times, those bullies are kept where they can do minimal harm. When violence might quell a problem rather than simply making it worse, bullies become very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about peasant business owners, should they work hard to make sure their business neither shrinks nor grows? Or is it just that a peasant can never become a patrician or something? </div> </div> </div>The mortal business owner is allowed to prosper, with reminders to shun unseemly greed and ambition, to bear in mind that their prosperity carries greater responsibility, and to remember that their prosperity is a gift from the Elemental Dragons, who can take it away if the mortal gives in to wickedness. But their prosperity has limits--if they're seen as too ambitious, they'll start losing business, suffering attacks from envious peers, paying exorbitant tax rates, and be bought out or run out of business by patricians or Dragon-Blooded. The monk doesn't personally do any of that, but might point out to interested parties that community strife is the obvious and inevitable consequence of peasants straying too far from their original role in a single lifetime. The monk might subtly or not-so-subtly inform a business owner, &quot;You've done enough. Now, instead of growing your business, you should focus on stability, or else put your skills to use for the Order or the Legions.&quot; And if the business owner ignores this sound advice, then they lose the monks' support, which is a death knell for any mortal-run business in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Edit: Eric ninja'd me. In all things, assume his words more clearly reflect the Perfect Hierarchy, as he is of a higher Coil of enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 07-03-2020, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:31:46-07:00","id":1400790,"title":"","content":"What if a Dragon-Blooded Dynast wanted to divorce her husband and marry her boyfriend (or girlfriend)? Would that violate the Immaculate Precepts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T14:52:23-07:00","id":1400827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400790#post1400790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if a Dragon-Blooded Dynast wanted to divorce her husband and marry her boyfriend (or girlfriend)? Would that violate the Immaculate Precepts?</div> </div> </div> </div>A marriage is annulled after <s>fifty years without a child (</s>25 years if you don't have any children<s>)</s>. So... not necessarily.<br /> <br /> But marriage is more of a political alliance than a religious union. The Dynast who wants to do a Prince Charles faces significant obstacles in the way of betraying their family obligations, which probably trumps the disapproval of the local monks.<br /> <br /> [EDIT]<br /> <br /> 3E has made some changes to 2E. See below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-07-2020, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T15:12:37-07:00","id":1400830,"title":"","content":"I guess I would put it that the Immaculate doesn't place a great emphasis so much on fixed nature and purpose for mortals, as much as that the social order ultimately flows harmoniously following the currents set by hierarchical superiors. <br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the peasant farmer wants to use wood for a door, table or fence, as he sees it best to suit the warp of the wood, and as it reveals itself to him and seeks his approval, but it is ill if it were to rebel against its shaping and his needs. It doesn't matter so much that mortals do not stay in the same job, but it does matter that any changes in roles are at least ratified, if not directed, by superiors in the order of reincarnation.<br /> <br /> (This is a lot like social mobility in theory in a lot of real world societies, though the Realm likely has more competence and consistency in getting closer to realising the social ideal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T08:20:00-07:00","id":1401347,"title":"","content":"Okay finally, I\u2019ve been looking around for a good example of what I think the rough scale of the imperial city is, and I think I found it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/a5/43/2f/a5432f7093eda9b7decba0a0037db145.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/a5/43/2f/a5432f7093eda9b7decba0a0037db145.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/a5/43/2f/a5432f7093eda9b7decba0a0037db145.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.pinimg.com/474x/a5/43/2f/a5432f7093eda9b7decba0a0037db145.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s not quite the right aesthetic, and I picture it less building to one massive pinnacle and more spread out among several huge landmark buildings, but I think that gives a good visual representation to let your mind imagine all the things that could be going on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T11:40:17-07:00","id":1401377,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I'm having no time right now but I promise I'll answer soon !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T12:27:49-07:00","id":1401381,"title":"","content":"Oh also cool are the Breaths of the immaculate order. The breath of Sextes Jylis takes care of Human Resources, public works, and environmental management, like forest planning and the like. The breath of pasiap covers the orders many holy construction projects as well as money management. The breath of Mela which is the military planning wing of the order. The breath of Hesiesh who take care of special projects and outside the box thinking. Finally the breath of Daana\u2019d, who focus on healthcare, education, public housing and humanitarian aid. <br /> <br /> The dark sides of them probably being along the lines of social surveillance, economic manipulation, warrior zealots, having way too much fun, and hard purging of heresy, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T19:35:02-07:00","id":1401419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1400827#post1400827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A marriage is annulled after fifty years without a child (25 years if you don't have any children).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure that is still a thing, in third edition, where Dynasts have <i>some</i> greater choice in marital options.<br /> <br /> Failure for a marriage to produce children produces social stigma, not political censure, and there are less drastic options for a sterile union to resolve their social expectation -- like adoption, surrogacy, or sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T20:27:47-07:00","id":1401424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1401419#post1401419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure that is still a thing, in third edition, where Dynasts have <i>some</i> greater choice in marital options.<br /> <br /> Failure for a marriage to produce children produces social stigma, not political censure, and there are less drastic options for a sterile union to resolve their social expectation -- like adoption, surrogacy, or sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>It *can* be annulled after 25 if you don't have children, according to the dragonblooded book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T23:08:01-07:00","id":1401435,"title":"","content":"Specifically:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought, page 96</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynastic Dragon-Blooded marriages usually last until one partner dies, but they can be ended by agreement of both parties\u2019 house matriarchs or an Imperial judge if the couple has failed to produce offspring after twenty-five years, or if one partner is found guilty of a serious crime such as attempting to harm or kill their spouse or children, murdering a Dragon-Blood, or committing treason. Beyond that, the only end to marriage is the death of one partner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which <b>is</b> different to the 2E stance I originally posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T00:17:29-07:00","id":1401634,"title":"","content":"The mountain in the center of the Isle is the Pole of Earth and it's infinitely deep. It quite literally holds up Creation too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T00:57:24-07:00","id":1401637,"title":"","content":"Another thing not entirely from the Realm book, but also from 1e. The Imperial Treasury is located over several treasure manses, but centrally is a sprawling compound of buildings, some dating back before the founding of the Realm. In there are winding corridors with back rooms full of paperwork dating back centuries, and ungodly secure vaults, some so secure that nobody currently alive can even open them.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of weird stuff there too, bound spirits and sorcerous enchantments.There's also a parliament of ghosts that convenes in one of the rooms sometimes on calibration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The organization itself is in trouble. People aren't keen to pay taxes to the government when they could skim it off the top for themselves in preparation for the coming war. So you have people rushing around trying to plug holes and figure out where all the damn money is going, fending off the depredations of the houses trying to gouge them out, and all set against a backdrop of a place so large, strange. ancient and labyrinthine that you could easily round the corner smack dab into a ghost flipping through the old ledgers from her past life, or have to walk past a vault door covered in jade eyes that follow you with unnerving precision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T06:32:22-07:00","id":1403652,"title":"","content":"So I'm back after a long pause. Sorry for answering late. <br /> <br /> Thanks for everyone mentioning many secondary schools and their specificities. This makes the cursus of the DB way more interesting to know there are many diversified options to follow. <br /> <br /> I appreciate the comments in response to DrLoveMonkey's response, I didn't conceive there was any social mobility possible in The Realm due to the &quot;Know your place&quot; mentality of the Order, but it's interesting to see it's a &quot;Know your place, and when to move when appropriate&quot; which makes it flexible enough that you can have dramatic social interaction with other people (trying to convince them that you were acting for the good of the community and not your own self-interest). <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I've read about the Breadth, but I'm very unsure of &quot;how they work&quot;. I get their purpose associated with each elements, but I can't quite figure out (or remember) : 1) What ranks are members of the Breadth in the Immaculate Order, 2) Are they working together with other breadths (Mage-like cabals, if you've played Mage) or only in the same Breadth, 3) Are they affected to one place and supervise it ? Or are they rather mobile and always deployed somewhere that is not their Monastery ? <br /> I like the idea of The Breadth, but I'm quite unsure of their place in the greater overall of the Immaculate Order. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> So I've successfully read Houses Cathak, Cynis and Ledaal (at least part of them), and I read a part reminiscent of a discussion few pages earlier with Isator Levi, &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ledaal ships home significant wealth from its sa- trapies, taking an active hand in their rulership&quot;. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We discussed how the Satrapy were quite autonomous concerning their self-governance, but the Ledaal seems specifically to interact a lot with the daily life of their Satrapies. Is this an exception or a normal application of their &quot;management of the garrison&quot; of the Satrapy ? </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T07:37:58-07:00","id":1403663,"title":"","content":"The breaths aren\u2019t one specific monk, they\u2019re administrative divisions in the order. Like the government ministries or different offices in a company. So you\u2019ll have monks in the Breath of Mela from all sorts of ranks and all over Creation, but they\u2019re all focused on the militant orders and combat training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:19:17-07:00","id":1403669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1403663#post1403663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The breaths aren\u2019t one specific monk, they\u2019re administrative divisions in the order. Like the government ministries or different offices in a company. So you\u2019ll have monks in the Breath of Mela from all sorts of ranks and all over Creation, but they\u2019re all focused on the militant orders and combat training.</div> </div> </div> </div>So my friendly local Monk that works alone covering 5 villages around could be a member of the Danaa'd breadth, and he was sent here because my region is known to give birth to regular annoying diseases (how the hell do you pronounce diseases in English ? disisis ?) and he's keeping an eye on it ? At first reading I really had the feeling they were kind of a specific elite force and I didn't know how to see their place in the order. I need to re-read the ranks of the Immaculate Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:41:23-07:00","id":1403672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1403669#post1403669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So my friendly local Monk that works alone covering 5 villages around could be a member of the Danaa'd breadth, and he was sent here because my region is known to give birth to regular annoying diseases (how the hell do you pronounce diseases in English ? disisis ?) and he's keeping an eye on it ? At first reading I really had the feeling they were kind of a specific elite force and I didn't know how to see their place in the order. I need to re-read the ranks of the Immaculate Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pronounce it dis-eez-es.<br /> <br /> And yes exactly, although each breath commands tens of thousands of monks on the blessed isle alone, so they can often deploy in greater numbers in a crisis. Also your bath in a breath isn\u2019t set, you can move between them as directed. So if there\u2019s an emergency healthcare crisis then high ranking officials in the Breath of Daana\u2019d direct monks in their Breath to concentrate in that area and provide support. If that healthcare crisis requires a big expenditure of the Order\u2019s money, they may talk to somebody from the Breath of Pasaip to release funds required to help. Or if the healthcare crisis is being caused by polluted water due to poorly managed waterways they bring in power from the Breath of Sextes Jylis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:42:33-07:00","id":1403673,"title":"","content":"The Breaths of the Immaculate Dragons are administrative/infrastructural arms of the Order. Breath members are not necessarily more elite than standard monks, but might be more specialized and project-focused. In fact, the Breath of Hesiesh is very much not-elite, providing a space where senescent, troublesome, and inauspicious monks can still be of use in unusual or counterintuitive projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:45:57-07:00","id":1403674,"title":"","content":"I see thanks for your answer. I have a clearer vision of how they fit now. I have the feeling that making a small campaign centered around specific aspects of the Breadth could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T04:00:45-07:00","id":1404745,"title":"","content":"So since it's the focus of another topic, does someone got interesting things to say about slaves ? Are there slaves of The Realm outside of the Blessed Isles ? Can they earn freedom ? In what kind of field do they work ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T05:03:41-07:00","id":1404751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404745#post1404745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there slaves of The Realm outside of the Blessed Isles ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Dynasts abroad will probably take their slaves with them, where practical and necessary. Don't forget that &quot;the Realm outside of the Blessed Isle&quot; consists of the loosely governed satrapies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, bullet points:<br /> <br /> * Slaves are almost always purchased or prisoners of war. Realm citizens can only be enslaved as punishment for some of the most severe crimes.<br /> * Only Dragon Blooded can own slaves, although they might delegate them to unExalted Dynasts or lease them to patricians.<br /> * Slaves have no rights guaranteed by the state, and are at the total mercy of their masters. Harming another Dynasts slaves is treated as property damage. They will typically be branded to identify their owners.<br /> * Slaves are allowed to possess their own property (although can only be permitted weapons when granted by their masters), but have no recourse to purchase their own freedom. That can only come with the decisions of their masters, but even Dynasts may only emancipate a single slave every year.<br /> * Current Realm law renders the children of slaves as automatically citizens of the Realm, rather than inheriting their parents slavery. This is promoted by House Cynis, to ensure that others require a steady stream of their product, as they hold the monopoly on that business; all buying and selling of slaves has to go through them.<br /> * Slaves can generally expect to be treated about as well as will allow them to perform their functions, at least as food and shelter go, but they'll invariably be subjected to brutal punishment if disobedient and the attitude of the Scarlet Dynasty typically entails some level of abuse for even the best-kept slave. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what kind of field do they work ?</div> </div> </div> </div>General domestic service in the sizable residences of the Exalted and additional work on their estates, whether that be labouring on the plantations or constructing the features. Slaves owned by the throne are the main workforce for the extension and maintenance of the national infrastructure. They're also used for the transportation of supplies in the Imperial Legions, those being among the better treated slaves to ensure that they don't disrupt logistics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T07:17:27-07:00","id":1404767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404745#post1404745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So since it's the focus of another topic, does someone got interesting things to say about slaves ? Are there slaves of The Realm outside of the Blessed Isles ? Can they earn freedom ? In what kind of field do they work ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm uses slaves across most fields -- Dynasts have slave physicians and tutors (though tutoring a Dynast's children is a prestigious position for Patrician tutors also). Essentially any position could be filled by a slave. Slaves can also have their material position improved by being enslaved and fed by the Realm rather than dying of starvation in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> Lastly, slaves aren't the lowest rung of Realm society. The dispossessed are peasants stripped of their rights and citizenship -- they may not own property, and citizens may do as they wish with them. They live as &quot;vagabonds&quot; and carry out &quot;backbreaking, poorly paid manual labor&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T03:08:02-07:00","id":1404900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404751#post1404751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, Dynasts abroad will probably take their slaves with them, where practical and necessary. Don't forget that &quot;the Realm outside of the Blessed Isle&quot; consists of the loosely governed satrapies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, bullet points:<br /> <br /> * Slaves are almost always purchased or prisoners of war. Realm citizens can only be enslaved as punishment for some of the most severe crimes.<br /> * Only Dragon Blooded can own slaves, although they might delegate them to unExalted Dynasts or lease them to patricians.<br /> * Slaves have no rights guaranteed by the state, and are at the total mercy of their masters. Harming another Dynasts slaves is treated as property damage. They will typically be branded to identify their owners.<br /> * Slaves are allowed to possess their own property (although can only be permitted weapons when granted by their masters), but have no recourse to purchase their own freedom. That can only come with the decisions of their masters, but even Dynasts may only emancipate a single slave every year.<br /> * Current Realm law renders the children of slaves as automatically citizens of the Realm, rather than inheriting their parents slavery. This is promoted by House Cynis, to ensure that others require a steady stream of their product, as they hold the monopoly on that business; all buying and selling of slaves has to go through them.<br /> * Slaves can generally expect to be treated about as well as will allow them to perform their functions, at least as food and shelter go, but they'll invariably be subjected to brutal punishment if disobedient and the attitude of the Scarlet Dynasty typically entails some level of abuse for even the best-kept slave.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> General domestic service in the sizable residences of the Exalted and additional work on their estates, whether that be labouring on the plantations or constructing the features. Slaves owned by the throne are the main workforce for the extension and maintenance of the national infrastructure. They're also used for the transportation of supplies in the Imperial Legions, those being among the better treated slaves to ensure that they don't disrupt logistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your most complete answer. For more precisions for bullet points by number : <br /> <br /> 1) Aren't Blessed Isles (which I assume are Realm Citizens) supposed to become Dispossessed (and so legally it's impossible to enslave them) when punished for the most severe crimes ? <br /> <br /> 3) and 4) I feel are in apparent contradiction. How can something with no right can be allowed to posses their own property ? Unless their own property is actually guaranteed by its owner I guess. <br /> <br /> 5) What happens of a child &quot;citizen of The Realm&quot; ? Does he become some sort of &quot;child of the Empress&quot; as could happen in some nations historically ? Or is it something totally different (they become child of the master that possess the slave) ?<br /> <br /> 5) Does House Cynis pass through other slaves traders outside of The Realm ? Or do they operate alone in acquiring them ? (for example, could they buy slaves directly to nations that are beyond the Threshold ?)<br /> <br /> 6) Are there laws (explicit or social) that protect, to a minimal, slaves ? Like you can't outright kill them, for example ? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I'm curious. Physicians are usually very high regarded positions in societies, with very specific and high level training. Do slaves get treated well (like, very well) materially with a prestigious position or should I expect the prestigious ones (physicians, savants, architects, etc ...) to usually live in a granary with poor material condition ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T04:52:26-07:00","id":1404908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404900#post1404900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Aren't Blessed Isles (which I assume are Realm Citizens) supposed to become Dispossessed (and so legally it's impossible to enslave them) when punished for the most severe crimes ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears not. Dispossession is generally imposed on entire communities rather than individuals, and tends to be particular to the crimes of rebellion and failure to pay taxes, or for the community in general displaying an overall disregard for the law. I presume that enslavement is a punishment that the Imperial judges have discretion to pronounce on heinous crimes such as rape or the most savage or insidious forms of murder. Maybe also certain forms of blasphemy.<br /> <br /> But no, dispossession has always been presented as a particular thing to deal with communities that, in whole or in part, express contempt for the authority of the Realm. It should be kept in mind that it can be a case in which the actions of a few can harm the many. Villages pay taxes as a unit, but everybody needs to make their share, and if some fail to provide and the rest don't have a surplus that will make the difference, all will be punished. And a family can be punished for the seditious conspiracies of their neighbours, even if they knew nothing of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) and 4) I feel are in apparent contradiction. How can something with no right can be allowed to posses their own property ? Unless their own property is actually guaranteed by its owner I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would take it that denial of personal possessions is not undertaken as a matter of course, but a slave has no recourse should their master opt to just confiscate it at will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) What happens of a child &quot;citizen of The Realm&quot; ? Does he become some sort of &quot;child of the Empress&quot; as could happen in some nations historically ? Or is it something totally different (they become child of the master that possess the slave) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not elaborated, and I suppose it varies. I would regard it as typical for them to fall under the custodianship of the Immaculate Order, as would likely be common with orphans, although many might find themselves adrift and unsupported in a manner that creates vagabonds and bandits. Still, that option might be seen as an embarrassment for Dynasts who are responsible for their existence. While adoption for mortal peasants is surely out of the question, a Dragon Blood might assign an agent to ensure that they are placed with accommodating peasant families, assuming there are not ones that proactively offer to take in such. And units of the Imperial Legions might periodically turn up looking for any that can be recruited.<br /> <br /> Still, I also presume that in a lot of cases, Dynasts just opt to keep their slaves gender segregated to minimise the opportunities for them to become pregnant. I they don't get to keep the children, I expect that it saves them on a bit of lost productivity and any expenses for seeing them off their property. For the sake of not being too grim, I presume that the status of being Realm citizens affords such children just enough protection under law that to allow them to be abandoned to die of exposure would... not necessarily be actionable against the Dynast (unless a judge or magistrate wanted to prove that the Dynast was aware and did not intervene, if not outright complicit), but constitutes a loss of face.<br /> <br /> Maybe some cases where the slaves set aside enough of what they have or receive to see the child to an age where they can begin to make their own way, at which point they shall have to. Or perhaps, even when not formally adopted, they might drift over into the portion of the household staff that is free. The child of a slave might end up becoming the servant of a servant to a Dynast; somebody to wait on or clean up after a clerk or guard or keeper of the winery or tutor.<br /> <br /> It's one of those things where I would find it to make the most sense for it to vary significantly based on circumstances, because there's probably little interest in formally establishing a uniform support system, and so it depends on the conditions of where one ends up. The child of a slave in a rich eastern prefecture with plenty, stability and a large quantity of well-established Immaculate institutions probably fares better than one who pops up among miners or people laying roads through some of the more marginal territory. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Does House Cynis pass through other slaves traders outside of The Realm ? Or do they operate alone in acquiring them ? (for example, could they buy slaves directly to nations that are beyond the Threshold ?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sure. Purchase of slaves for transit to the Blessed Isle will be among the businesses that give them the best relationship with the Guild of the Scarlet Dynasty. Association with the Realm promotes slavery among the satrapies (in the cases of those run by House Cynis, the satrap probably often outright encourages the authorities in this, and maybe even incentivizes it by pointing it out as a good way to bring in Cynis revenue that can be turned back around to pay the tribute), and the knowledge of that will surely attract other slaver businesses.<br /> <br /> I would say developing satrapies as markets to attract foreign vendors is a lot more common than a Cynis scion venturing out to purchase slaves held in a market beyond their control (for one thing, they absorb even more of the cost of transporting them back home), but maybe occasionally some member of the family struggling to find a niche elsewhere in the business might go that extra mile to try and get a leg up. I would say even that most typically requires places with well-established and well-stocked slave markets to shop around in, rather than meeting directly with vendors; Nexus would make sense in particular as a place that sees its fair share of Cynis.<br /> <br /> But I can also think of other scenarios in which it does make sense to buy directly from a vendor, particularly if they were en route to a different market; intercepting a shipment before it reaches market and purchasing wholesale can not only be an underhanded way of getting some quickly and for relatively low price at a time when your stock might be low, it also might be done with the intention of undercutting a rival market or trader. Enough gets to Nexus that the family still goes there to buy, but there are several reasons to prefer that less stock goes to Nexus than does to your satrapies. That's a case where I imagine it's all running on elaborate calculations; if the Nexus market can be competitive enough (or Guild factors might arrange to buy up most of them before you can arrive and then sell it on with a huge mark up, because you're a Great House of the Scarlet Dynasty, surely you can afford it) that in some years that it may actually be cheaper to intercept a shipment ahead of time and redirect it home, paying for the food and the slave drivers all the way. Or there might be financial loss but political capital in acquiring slaves in a manner that does not put money into the economy of enemies; coin spent in Nexus can help fund the defiance of Lookshy and heresy of Great Forks. You'll lose money, but selling the slaves at the end still means that you lose <i>less</i> money, and that might be a case where what you're really spending it on is the goodwill of the Houses, the throne and the Order.<br /> <br /> This distribution of interests is what you need hundreds of Exalted for. And members of House Cynis are in some level of competition with one another as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Are there laws (explicit or social) that protect, to a minimal, slaves ? Like you can't outright kill them, for example ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reference to such, and it would seem contrary to the established character of the thing for there to be. The lives of slaves are generally protected by them being a source of revenue for their masters; the point at which inadequacy or resistance makes them wholly incapable of serving that function means that the last way for them to provide for that is to serve as an example to the other slaves, and many Dynasts probably want to be sure that leaves an impression. I can't see other authorities being interested in curbing that.<br /> <br /> Killing slaves on a whim or for pleasure might not be proscribed, but I would regard it as the kind of thing that disturbs other Dynasts, which might reduce one's profile a lot but maybe has to be extremely severe to be outright shunned over it. <br /> <br /> I personally once imagined a scenario in which rival Dynasts at a gala would engage in sharp-tongued banter with one another, and one makes a comment that elicits an involuntary but audible chuckle from an attending slave. It seemed to me that person would be doomed by such, as Dynast etiquette would demand that the person who made the humourous statement be the one to immediately see to their punishment, which is likely to be savage and motivated; I picture many a Dynast that would genuinely dislike the person they would mock while being deeply disgusted at a mortal of such low stature daring to openly laugh at them. You of course still pay for the slave.<br /> <br /> (I can see a relationship between some masters and slaves that is cordial in a manner where the Dynast shares witticisms about their peers that the slave laughs at, but that stuff is best kept in private; if such slaves are part of your entourage in public, they'd be best not seen laughing along at any barbs)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physicians are usually very high regarded positions in societies, with very specific and high level training. Do slaves get treated well (like, very well) materially with a prestigious position or should I expect the prestigious ones (physicians, savants, architects, etc ...) to usually live in a granary with poor material condition ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Physicians and similar slaves (I don't believe they'd ever be used as architects) are expensive and assigned to sensitive positions, so keeping them in good conditions is just practical (although they might be sent to the inferior quarters for a stint if there's a need to discipline them). Bad conditions are for slaves perceived as cheap and plentiful.<br /> <br /> (Granaries are for grain, not people)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T05:09:38-07:00","id":1404909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404908#post1404908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Granaries are for grain, not people)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was thinking of stables, you know the place where the bad rich person put their nice hardworking slave because whatever ... in stories. <br /> <br /> I like your answer about the children of slaves, it gives a lot of space to be creative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T07:47:06-07:00","id":1404920,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the material on slavery in the Realm was largely drawn from Greek and Roman slavery; most of these questions can be resolved by seeing how they were addressed by real-world slaveholding cultures in the classical era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T08:16:52-07:00","id":1404924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404920#post1404920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the material on slavery in the Realm was largely drawn from Greek and Roman slavery; most of these questions can be resolved by seeing how they were addressed by real-world slaveholding cultures in the classical era.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting remark because it was my first thought when I envisaged the slaves in The Realm, but then the fact that they could not earn their freedom made me think I was wrong. Or maybe it's just my historical knowledge that sucks ? I was pretty sure Greeko-romans slaves could buy their freedom with either money or years of service (or maybe they could do it in some states/periods and not in others ?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T08:58:44-07:00","id":1404926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404924#post1404924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting remark because it was my first thought when I envisaged the slaves in The Realm, but then the fact that they could not earn their freedom made me think I was wrong. Or maybe it's just my historical knowledge that sucks ? I was pretty sure Greeko-romans slaves could buy their freedom with either money or years of service (or maybe they could do it in some states/periods and not in others ?).</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that varied based on time, place, status, and circumstances. In any case, as noted, those were inspirational sources but were not strictly adhered to; using them as a resource should answer many questions but is not guaranteed to answer all of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T08:59:29-07:00","id":1404927,"title":"","content":"Greece and Rome both have a very long history; policies as regards how they treat slaves are something that will have varied from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T09:06:41-07:00","id":1404928,"title":"","content":"I guess that makes sense. Thanks for your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T12:06:30-07:00","id":1404952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404900#post1404900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) What happens of a child &amp;quot;citizen of The Realm&amp;quot; ? Does he become some sort of &amp;quot;child of the Empress&amp;quot; as could happen in some nations historically ? Or is it something totally different (they become child of the master that possess the slave) ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm states that children of the dispossessed are peasants, but that their prospects are limited unless they are given over to Immaculate Orphanages.<br /> <br /> I imagine the children of slaves remain the children of their parents but are peasants rather than slaves. Their prospects in life are going to vary based on the whims of their parent's masters, I'd imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T06:02:33-07:00","id":1405555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1404924#post1404924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pretty sure Greeko-romans slaves could buy their freedom with either money or years of service (or maybe they could do it in some states/periods and not in others ?).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Republican era, domestic and professional slaves, particularly those in an urban environment, were more likely to acquire means or good standing to receive freedom, although sometimes needing that to be granted in the wills of their deceased masters. There were enough of them to form a whole social class in Rome; it was not merely legal, it was part of the expectations of what would be done with such slaves (although popular sentiment as expressed in surviving writing still mostly held that a person currently a slave had a lessened humanity). Slaves who worked in fields and mines were much less likely to possess property or be treated well, and for mining in particular had very poor life expectancy. This was during an era when Roman legions were likely to be conducting active campaigns all across the frontiers that continuously brought in more slaves.<br /> <br /> (Sometimes more slaves than could be fully handled; a lot of the people who rose up in the Servile Wars of Spartacus fame had been brought in by Roman success against a group of Germanic tribes that had been particularly threatening a few decades before. A large influx of people that had been proud and successful enemies.)<br /> <br /> Starting with the imperial era, legal avenues for freeing slaves were significantly curtailed, and officials promoted the idea that it should be lessened. Expansion of the provinces was being slowed down dramatically, and that was going to greatly reduce the number of slaves being brought in at a time when they were still an integral part of the economy. That's a period where the position of slaves becomes a lot less dynamic.<br /> <br /> I could see the value of slaves in the Realm as occupying a space somewhere in the middle of those, and with adjustments made in regards to some of the other important differences in class structure and prevailing religious attitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T07:50:59-07:00","id":1405574,"title":"","content":"From my understanding slavery in the Roman mines was treated basically like an extended death sentence. Like we could stone or crucify you but we don\u2019t need a public execution right now so we might as well get some work out of you before you die. <br /> <br /> I think my favourite might be slave accountants though. <br /> <br /> \u201cDamnit Petros, what do you mean it\u2019s no longer profitable to ship our lavender harvest? I just successfully petitioned to have the tariffs removed!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes but the shipping costs just doubled, the shipping company owned by house Cynis cites increasing piracy as the reason.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBah! I should sell you to Cynis Berne so you can give her all the bad news!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe couldn\u2019t afford me. Especially not after we offer up our lucrative lavender deal to V\u2019Neef Ilara to cut her out of the deal entirely.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that legal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEh, technically? It depends who owns the lavender farms.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. I\u2019ll draft a letter to my wife\u2019s cousin right away.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T10:00:17-07:00","id":1405604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1405574#post1405574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my favourite might be slave accountants though. </div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Do you trust your wife?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T16:41:23-07:00","id":1405692,"title":"","content":"One feature of Greco-Roman slavery that the Realm distinctly lacks is the capacity to sell oneself into slavery. Or at least... there are possibly people outside of the Realm who do so, but it's not quite so prominently featured.<br /> <br /> In Rome, your enslaved clerk or accountant or whomever is probably just a professional (often from Greece) who had some bad debts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T22:04:14-07:00","id":1405748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1405692#post1405692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One feature of Greco-Roman slavery that the Realm distinctly lacks is the capacity to sell oneself into slavery. Or at least... there are possibly people outside of the Realm who do so, but it's not quite so prominently featured.<br /> <br /> In Rome, your enslaved clerk or accountant or whomever is probably just a professional (often from Greece) who had some bad debts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, considering that, we\u2019re do they enslave people with much better educations? Do they kidnap them from satrapies? Enslave then as children and then educate them? They\u2019re physicians, teachers, accountants, entertainers and whatever else, they\u2019ve got to learn that somewhere. <br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s used as a punishment? Like you embezzled X amount of money from the treasury, but instead of executing or imprisoning you, you get to put your skills to work as a slave accountant. Although I\u2019m not sure about the demand for resentful confirmed criminals are, especially sending them back to work in exactly the place they previously helped commit crimes in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T01:12:05-07:00","id":1405755,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's the brightest of the Threshold who get creamed away as tribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T04:11:09-07:00","id":1405912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1405748#post1405748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, considering that, we\u2019re do they enslave people with much better educations? Do they kidnap them from satrapies? Enslave then as children and then educate them? They\u2019re physicians, teachers, accountants, entertainers and whatever else, they\u2019ve got to learn that somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm finding myself uncertain about how many of these are used as slaves in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Take physicians for example, since that's one that is described in detail. There are hardly any slave physicians in the Realm, because being tended to by those is reserved for the elderly Exalted, of which there are few.<br /> <br /> ...I think. Hmm, at first I read it in those terms, and that would still hold up if one didn't hold the following paragraphs needing to keep qualifying themselves, but still, it comes across as a bit more ambiguous. But saying they &quot;maintain personal doctors, especially as they age&quot; implies an expectation that they'll have doctors before they age, but handling ailments is described as the reserve of the Exalted physician, and do younger Dynasts even typically have the kinds of ailments that slaves seem to be retained for? Okay, put a pin in that one.<br /> <br /> So, other things that educated and professional slaves would be employed for, mostly several kinds of administrative duty. It may be that there are occasional references to slaves being used for those that I can't recall offhand, but the core information of the Realm says that these are specifically the functions of the patrician class. The landed ancient Roman might use a slave to oversee the estate he's absent from, but descriptions of the Realm suggest that Dynasts will (perhaps <u>must</u>) employ a patrician.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if the educated slave in the Realm is primarily the one for entertainment purposes.<br /> <br /> In any case, as for where they come from, there are references to House Cynis putting down the capital to train such people to fetch a higher price, but a big part would be the claiming as prisoners of war. Even in a captured army, there are liable to be people with specialised skills in medicine and management and the use of instruments, and if you've sacked a town or city then you have your pick. I don't expect residents of the satrapies to often be taken as slaves, but rather are acquiring such slaves from their neighbours, who end up in the position either through debt peonage or being taken in wars or raids. An educated or professional person probably resides in a settlement and is thus more resistant to being claimed by roaming slavers than people working the open fields (or foraging in them), but not completely so.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't think the Realm kidnaps them from the satrapies, but they'll buy them from people who bought them from people who kidnapped them elsewhere. At least typically, officially; I can presume that just about any situation of slavery contains its fair share of opportunists who'll use underhanded means to bundle somebody they think will fetch money away to a slave market even when that's a crime, in the manner of Solomon Northup. Free black people being kidnapped for slavery was perhaps not a danger afflicting a sizable portion of the population, but still a persistent danger. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it\u2019s used as a punishment? Like you embezzled X amount of money from the treasury, but instead of executing or imprisoning you, you get to put your skills to work as a slave accountant. Although I\u2019m not sure about the demand for resentful confirmed criminals are, especially sending them back to work in exactly the place they previously helped commit crimes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enslavement for crimes is a part of the Realm sure, but I wouldn't expect to the degree that it is the expected source of them. It's more like this being an expected outcome for such criminals, and that happens to make them part of the tapestry of slave origins.<br /> <br /> The argument of &quot;the resentful criminal makes a bad worker&quot; is pretty silly because... just about every slave is resentful. Heck, when people presume that the professional slave will deliberately do a bad job of it that they don't apply to the agricultural slave, it even ends up being a tad elitist. And sure, evidence does seem to suggest that there are instances in which plantation slaves in the Americas would do as bad a job as they could get away with in protest of the people owning them.<br /> <br /> But such instances need to be counterbalanced with the matter of what slaveowners might do to impress upon slaves that doing this presents a significant risk to them. In the case of the convicted white collar criminal, if the fact that it was behaviour that has destroyed their life was not enough to dissuade them, being show the crucifixions, the breaking on the wheel, the mutilations, those might put them off (also, what are you going to do with embezzled money that won't be quickly noticed).<br /> <br /> Evidence would suggest that there have always been chattel slaves who resisted their circumstances to the best extent that they were capable, but there have also always been plenty of slaves who, of their own accord, decided that it was not worth doing things that might make their lives even worse, and slaves who were effectively traumatised into submission.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:22:26-07:00","id":1407890,"title":"","content":"So I just finished reading all the Great Houses from DB and the Magistracy from The Realm. I'm very interested in the Magistracy from a ST point of view because it allows for players to explore The Realm society without being totally bounded by it (plus it allows to play &quot;the good guys&quot; etc ...). However I don't see how to make a campaign with a group of Magistrates since they usually work alone, or only with mortal archons. <br /> <br /> Any of you would have campaigns ideas to work around a magistrate/group of magistrates ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:40:38-07:00","id":1407891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1407890#post1407890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just finished reading all the Great Houses from DB and the Magistracy from The Realm. I'm very interested in the Magistracy from a ST point of view because it allows for players to explore The Realm society without being totally bounded by it (plus it allows to play &amp;quot;the good guys&amp;quot; etc ...). However I don't see how to make a campaign with a group of Magistrates since they usually work alone, or only with mortal archons. <br /> <br /> Any of you would have campaigns ideas to work around a magistrate/group of magistrates ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only one Magistrate in my game, but maybe I can still help you:<br /> <br /> Our Magistrate was tracking down shipments of seditious books that were making their way into the Blessed Isle. This led her to a Sondok cult.<br /> <br /> Another PC, in a different part of the world, found their Satrapy under attack by a demonologist who found a way to beckon Sondok unbound into creation.<br /> <br /> Another PC ventured to Malfeas to find a weapon to use against the Lunars attacking his Satrapy, where servants of Sondok killed his boyfriend.<br /> <br /> The last PC had her life saved when Sondok killed the Lunar that was just about to kill her.<br /> <br /> Now the PCs are all trying to track down Sondok.<br /> <br /> The same could happen in your game -- seemingly unrelated incidents could build to a vast conspiracy. Don't forget also that the Magistrates are on the back-foot in RY768 (no Empress to protect them, vengeful enemies gearing up for a civil war). A group of relatively young Magistrates might just band together for protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T05:46:40-07:00","id":1407906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1407891#post1407891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget also that the Magistrates are on the back-foot in RY768 (no Empress to protect them, vengeful enemies gearing up for a civil war). A group of relatively young Magistrates might just band together for protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the young ones, I think. Particularly with the introduction of the idea that V'neef is turning her prefecture into a sanctuary for them. There's a vested interest for them to work in groups while they're at risk from vengeful Dynasts, particularly if they can figure out a new Empress to support that would be favourable towards them.<br /> <br /> And not just in terms of somebody who'll resume business as it was before the Time of Tumult. I think a valid plot point for magistrates would be a few who would want to pursue being elevated to a new power in the Realm. Still responsible for enforcement and auditing, just with a lot more fringe benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:10:09-07:00","id":1407969,"title":"","content":"Agree on all counts. I was merely presuming the default character creation rules being followed resulting in <i>relatively</i> inexperienced Magistrates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:14:44-07:00","id":1408041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1407969#post1407969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree on all counts. I was merely presuming the default character creation rules being followed resulting in <i>relatively</i> inexperienced Magistrates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd prefer to make them play young Magistrates, but I definitively would use the V'neef to play as the common denominator to assemble them and give them purpose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:35:44-07:00","id":1408168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1407969#post1407969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree on all counts. I was merely presuming the default character creation rules being followed resulting in <i>relatively</i> inexperienced Magistrates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, of course. I didn't read deeply enough into the query about games based around groups of them.<br /> <br /> I'd even say that in the absence of the Empress, there's room for developments in which magistrates decide to take it on themselves to deputise new people of sufficient character, or even some young people in the Realm appointing themselves to the role.<br /> <br /> I think Pasiap's Stair represents a possibility for such a thing; a group of outcastes who took the coin when they were children, only for the Empress to disappear halfway through their training. They've graduated now, but the legions have no place for them. I can see such as those, indoctrinated towards loyalty to the Realm and having likely grown up with some admiration for the stories of the magistrates (maybe even personally witnessing such for one or two of them) gravitating towards that office while the empire is falling apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T10:10:58-07:00","id":1408183,"title":"","content":"Who manages the Nine Rigorous Examinations ? Specific ministries ? Also, what do you think is the proportion of Exalted Dynasts in the Ministries ? One or two in the important Ministries ? More ? I have the feeling scions from Great Houses are not supposed to go into the Ministries but this seems contradictory with the importance the Ministries seems to have in The Realm.<br /> <br /> Also, to keep the initial idea of the topic relevant : Any of you invented a Ministry they would like to share ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T18:09:58-07:00","id":1408296,"title":"","content":"I think a couple hundred Dynasts might accumulate in the Ministries. Primarily in the midst prestigious ones, but you get a few in key strategic ones such as weights and measures.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's anything barring them, but that many Dynasts find it an uninviting prospect; it has much honour, but few rewards compared to using the family resources to make your own way. I expect many matriarchs are averse to the loyalty and service of their scions going so directly to the throne.<br /> <br /> I expect there is a balancing act between the bureaucracy, who are organs of the control of the Empress, and the Great Houses in possession of much wealth and many specialised remits. Mortal bureaucrats might sometimes speak with her authority, but I suspect in most cases it's practical to speak to the Houses through intermediaries such as patricians or the unExalted.<br /> <br /> The ministries are important sure, but I imagine most of their day-to-day functions in keeping the empire running are a tedium that Dynasts are content to find chugging along without them, but to their benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T01:41:16-07:00","id":1408466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1408296#post1408296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a couple hundred Dynasts might accumulate in the Ministries. Primarily in the midst prestigious ones, but you get a few in key strategic ones such as weights and measures.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's anything barring them, but that many Dynasts find it an uninviting prospect; it has much honour, but few rewards compared to using the family resources to make your own way. I expect many matriarchs are averse to the loyalty and service of their scions going so directly to the throne.<br /> <br /> I expect there is a balancing act between the bureaucracy, who are organs of the control of the Empress, and the Great Houses in possession of much wealth and many specialised remits. Mortal bureaucrats might sometimes speak with her authority, but I suspect in most cases it's practical to speak to the Houses through intermediaries such as patricians or the unExalted.<br /> <br /> The ministries are important sure, but I imagine most of their day-to-day functions in keeping the empire running are a tedium that Dynasts are content to find chugging along without them, but to their benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for your answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T07:41:49-07:00","id":1409134,"title":"","content":"How do you handle a character acquiring the power of the Realm Defense Grid ? He can basically erase anything he wants, but it will also destroy everything that's around that thing ? Any tips or ideas for consequences/drawbacks ? Have you ever had a player that had the occasion to use it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:03:52-07:00","id":1409198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409134#post1409134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you handle a character acquiring the power of the Realm Defense Grid ? He can basically erase anything he wants, but it will also destroy everything that's around that thing ? Any tips or ideas for consequences/drawbacks ? Have you ever had a player that had the occasion to use it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No \u2018in my game\u2019 answer, but my understanding is that using the RDG damages the Blessed Isle, with more damage as you strike further out and as strike harder. So it\u2019s usually only politically ok to use on the Isle, at \u2018destroy small town\u2019 level. Although in a game, I think I\u2019d emphasize the command center aspect of the manse. Imagine how much information could be in Norad, plus say maps locating weapons caches, plus whatever personal gear a defense-minded Solar might keep around.<br /> <br /> re slaves: if my books are correct, common practice for Romans was to conquer a rebellious town, sell whole population including the skilled people. <br /> <br /> magistrates: no reason a group of Magistrates couldn\u2019t form a Sworn Hearth (that the current term?), to handle a big problem. It\u2019s dangerous gathering in a group, but more dangerous to go solo and lose. I doubt the Emptess would take a group and make them a group of magistrates, more likely to promote the group but send each one to different trouble spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:18:24-07:00","id":1409202,"title":"","content":"Reading the Realm for first or second time, what strikes me is how it now feels like a continent instead of a country. Prefectures feel closer to counties than states, with many controlled by Patricians and some with no local population of Dragonblooded, just seeing an itinerant Immaculate every so often. There is mention of some regions that were settled by Contagion refugees and still have elements of the old culture, so definitely could have towns with odd customs. Probably more subtle, closer to the Innsmouth Look than \u2018extra holifay that was originally worshipping a Solar\u2019. Enough First Age stuff turning up there\u2019s a special Ministey to handle it. And the Isle is big enough to have and need more than four schools.<br /> <br /> <br /> A specific bit I likeis bottom of page 19. There are areas of unpopulated or scarey wilderness. In other words, places for cautious Anathema to hide, or rogue gods who need put in their place. (moreso in the last few years as the bronze faction Fate monitoring operation has had problems)<br /> <br /> etc etc. Realm feels like a big place where you can adventure, not \u201cthe place with all the Dragonbloods living practically on top of each other\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:08:55-07:00","id":1409218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409202#post1409202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">etc etc. Realm feels like a big place where you can adventure, not \u201cthe place with all the Dragonbloods living practically on top of each other\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the name &quot;Blessed Isle&quot; feels like a holdover from previous editions that doesn't really fit anymore. It might be more accurate to call it &quot;the Blessed Continent&quot; instead, or maybe even &quot;the Blessed World&quot; (which would have a connotation similar to the First World in real life).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:36:30-07:00","id":1409225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409218#post1409218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the name &amp;quot;Blessed Isle&amp;quot; feels like a holdover from previous editions that doesn't really fit anymore. It might be more accurate to call it &amp;quot;the Blessed Continent&amp;quot; instead, or maybe even &amp;quot;the Blessed World&amp;quot; (which would have a connotation similar to the First World in real life).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I like the name &quot;Blessed Isle&quot;, might I suggest &quot;Blessed Realm&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T21:07:59-07:00","id":1409279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409198#post1409198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sworn Hearth (that the current term?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're close.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sworn Fellowship&quot; is the default term. &quot;Hearth&quot; is an alternative term, particularly used in the context of a Fellowship with a defined home base or place of origin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T02:49:05-07:00","id":1409317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409218#post1409218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be more accurate to call it &quot;the Blessed Continent&quot; instead, or maybe even &quot;the Blessed World&quot; <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those don't sound very euphonic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T05:45:30-07:00","id":1409335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409317#post1409317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those don't sound very euphonic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've no doubts there could be better sounding names. I'm just saying that calling a landmass the size of a small continent an &quot;Isle&quot; probably contributes to the perception of it as a smaller place than it really is. It's kind of like if you took Australia and called it &quot;the Austral Isle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-20-2020, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:08:27-07:00","id":1409390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409335#post1409335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've no doubts there could be better sounding names. I'm just saying that calling a landmass the size of a small continent an &quot;Isle&quot; probably contributes to the perception of it as a smaller place than it really is. It's kind of like if you took Australia and called it &quot;the Austral Isle&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>People do still call Australia an island continent though. I think that both continent and island are so il-defined a lot of the times that Blessed Isle can get away with it. It just needs to be reminded that well, it's an &quot;isle&quot; in teh sense South America use to be before it crashed into Panama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T15:47:18-07:00","id":1409429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409279#post1409279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Sworn Fellowship&amp;quot; is the default term.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is Sworn Kinship.<br /> <br /> Fellowship is more of a sidereal thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T19:39:14-07:00","id":1409446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398566-tell-me-about-the-realm?p=1409429#post1409429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is Sworn Kinship.<br /> <br /> Fellowship is more of a sidereal thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops! I was like &quot;I'm 70% sure and that's probably enough to not have to look it up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}